nray-houdini","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf9e8673-d385-4d8d-a397-0f8f64be7168","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:21:16.507Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"cf9e8673-d385-4d8d-a397-0f8f64be7168","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ESWRNJSjWeMPw8RY5vhESm","type":"tool_result","content":"**1. Non-differentiable nodes replaced by proxies**\n- MATch generators: Brick, Stripe, Scratches, Tile (Paraboloid), Tile (Brick), and Arc Pavement.\n- Hu et al. (2022) framework: Point Process Texture Basis Functions (PPTBF).\n\n**2. Proxy architecture, data, and training**\n- Architecture: a modified StyleGAN2. Parameters pass through fully connected layers into an intermediate W space, which feeds AdaIN layers. Noise inputs are removed, making the network deterministic.\n- Data: 300,000 synthetic 256×256 images per MATch proxy, sampled independently per parameter using the mean and standard deviation of artist-used values from Substance Source (7000+ graphs). PPTBF used the released dataset plus 500,000 resampled mask maps.\n- Loss: L = λ0·L1 + λ1·L_feat + λ2·L_style (+ λ3·L_Adv), with λ0 = λ2 = 1 and λ1 = 10. L_feat is an L1 difference of VGG19 features. L_style is an L1 difference of Gram matrices. λ3 = 0 by default and is greater than 0 for stochastic generators. L_Adv is a cross-entropy critic with R1 regularization (γ = 10).\n- Training: 60 epochs, about 2–3 days on one RTX 3090. Adam, learning rate 0.0025, batch size 32, parameters normalized to [0, 1]. The discriminator uses Adam at learning rate 1e-3. Each proxy is under 100 MB.\n\n**3. Multi-stage optimization**\n- Stage I (pre-optimization): optimizes filter parameters θf only, with generators fixed, using a multi-scale Gram/style L1 loss at 256, 128, and 64 px. Learning rate 0.002.\n- Stage II (global): first samples 500 generator initializations and picks the best by grayscale deep-feature L1 loss. Then optimizes all θ with L = feature L1 + α·Gram L1, α = 0.05, multi-resolution. Adam (β = (0.9, 0.999)), initial learning rate 0.02, halved every 200 steps.\n- Stage III (post-optimization): swaps proxies back to the real generators and fine-tunes θf with the Stage I style loss at learning rate 0.002.\n- Total: about 1000 steps for the full optimization. The paper does not give per-stage step counts.\n\n**4. Structure vs. appearance**\n- Structure: generator parameters θg, driven through the proxy in Stage II.\n- Appearance (color, roughness, and similar): filter parameters θf, optimized in Stage I and refined in Stage III.\n- Stage II's initialization uses grayscale images because color and roughness are already set by then.\n\n**5. Runtime**\n- Proxy dataset generation: 5–10 hours. Proxy training: 2–3 days.\n- Full optimization: 3–5 minutes for 1000 steps (MATch alone: 2–3 minutes).\n- PPTBF case: about 30 seconds versus 20 minutes for Hu et al., a stated 40× speedup.\n\n**6. Limitations and failure cases**\n- Complex graphs can reach local minima. The paper says manual graph simplification can help.\n- The loss does not match elements per pixel, so local details are missed (e.g., wood knots). Scale can also be off (a 7×7 target produced a 6×7 result).\n- Proxies do not reproduce patterns outside the artist-derived parameter range (e.g., too many bricks).\n- If the initial graph is not expressive enough, the method fails.\n- Filter nodes with discrete or random behavior, such as FX-map, remain non-differentiable."}]},"uuid":"e0c69ee3-6a78-4153-a6e3-fab5d314fde4","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:21:28.728Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2403a780-692d-4353-9013-a655df5b187b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf9e8673-d385-4d8d-a397-0f8f64be7168","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude