{"parentUuid":"7333b3ff-b949-4e1f-a0bd-1173ed49e596","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bchnyjyb1wroFHDA4rHwfi","type":"tool_result","content":"**DiffMat** is a PyTorch-based library for differentiable procedural material modeling. It reproduces the compositing graph system of Adobe Substance 3D Designer so that material parameters can be optimized with auto-differentiation. Its main use is fitting material graphs to captured photos.\n\n**Node types:** The page does not give a total count of supported nodes. It organizes node definitions into function graph nodes, FX-Map graph nodes, noise generator nodes, and other generator/filter nodes. It also mentions Quadrant nodes with atomic pattern functions. A separate `incomplete_nodes.md` lists nodes with partial support.\n\n**Translation:** DiffMat converts `*.sbs` files into differentiable computation graphs. A translator module handles the material graph, function graphs, FX-Maps, nodes, and parameters. Graphs are then compiled into a differentiable program. Unsupported nodes have their output textures pre-cached with Substance tools.\n\n**Optimizers:**\n- **Gradient-based:** `Optimizer` tunes continuous node parameters against a target image.\n- **Hybrid (mixed-integer):** `HybridOptimizer` optimizes both continuous and discrete parameters.\n- **Gradient-free alternatives (optional):** Bayesian optimization (scikit-optimize, Ax) and simulated annealing (simanneal).\n- **Sampler:** `ParamSampler` randomly samples or perturbs continuous parameters to create variations.\n\n**Loss functions:** The page mentions a modular loss function in `metric.py`. Optional image-space metrics include LPIPS and L\\*a\\*b\\* (via kornia). It does not describe the default loss in detail.\n\n**Papers:**\n- *MATch: Differentiable Material Graphs for Procedural Material Capture* (SIGGRAPH Asia 2020). This is the original work.\n- *End-to-End Procedural Material Capture with Proxy-Free Mixed-Integer Optimization* (SIGGRAPH 2023). The page calls this the \"latest paper.\" It states that DiffMat v2 no longer relies on proprietary tools for noise textures.\n- Works that build on DiffMat include PhotoScene, Node Graph Optimization Using Differentiable Proxies, Generating Procedural Materials from Text or Image Prompts, PSDR-Room, and Procedural Material Generation with Reinforcement Learning.\n\n**Requirements:**\n- **Substance tools:** Adobe Substance 3D Designer or the Substance 3D Automation Toolkit (SAT) is needed in practice. DiffMat uses its `sbscooker` and `sbsrender` tools to pre-cache textures for unsupported nodes, and implementing all generator nodes natively is impractical.\n- **Software:** Python ≥ 3.7, PyTorch ≥ 1.11.0, Torchvision ≥ 0.12.0, and Taichi-lang ≥ 1.3.0, plus NumPy, SciPy, pandas, imageio, pyyaml, and setuptools.\n- **Hardware:** A GPU with at least 16GB VRAM is recommended for complex materials. CPU use requires the `-c` flag.\n\n**Limitations:**\n- Only square textures are supported.\n- The SBS file must contain a single material graph with no custom dependent graphs.\n- Some non-atomic material and function nodes are unsupported.\n- Some rarely used features of supported nodes are omitted.\n- VRAM usage is high.\n\n**License:** DiffMat is released under a joint noncommercial license from MIT and Adobe."}]},"uuid":"ec9b69aa-162e-492b-816d-b11bc937372b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:14.879Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ca3eaaeb-f6e8-46f2-8f94-b19baeaecdb3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7333b3ff-b949-4e1f-a0bd-1173ed49e596","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userT