{"parentUuid":"f4819cd4-501f-4e63-9268-f4bb9e840842","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G2v6h1sVhh9gyFUeDo5rNL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Generating Procedural Materials from Text or Image Prompts\" Hu Guerrero Hašan Rushmeier Deschaintre arXiv 2023\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Generating Procedural Materials from Text or Image Prompts\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.13172\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.13172\"},{\"title\":\"Generating Procedural Materials from Text or Image Prompts\",\"url\":\"https://deepai.org/publication/generating-procedural-materials-from-text-or-image-prompts\"},{\"title\":\"generating procedural materials from text or image prompts\",\"url\":\"https://research.adobe.com/publication/generating-procedural-materials-from-text-or-image-prompts/\"},{\"title\":\"generating procedural materials from text or image prompts\",\"url\":\"https://graphics.cs.yale.edu/sites/default/files/generating_procedural_materials_from_text_or_image_prompts.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"par.nsf.gov\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10485688\"},{\"title\":\"Generating Procedural Materials from Text or Image Prompts\",\"url\":\"https://graphics.cs.yale.edu/node/250\"},{\"title\":\"generating procedural materials from text or image prompts by hu guerrero hasan rushmeier and deschaintre\",\"url\":\"https://history.siggraph.org/learning/generating-procedural-materials-from-text-or-image-prompts-by-hu-guerrero-hasan-rushmeier-and-deschaintre\"},{\"title\":\"“Generating Procedural Materials From Text or Image Prompts” by Hu, Guerrero, Hasan, Rushmeier and Deschaintre\",\"url\":\"https://history.siggraph.org/?p=132293\"}]\n\nThe paper you're looking for is arXiv:2304.13172, submitted April 25, 2023 under cs.GR. The authors are Yiwei Hu, Paul Guerrero, Miloš Hašan, Holly Rushmeier, and Valentin Deschaintre. It was published at SIGGRAPH 2023 and is listed there as an accepted technical paper.\n\nThe work addresses node graphs, which are used for material design in computer graphics. The authors propose a model that generates multiple procedural material graphs from image prompts, text prompts, or with no conditioning, and it can also complete partially built graphs. Its generative model can produce multiple procedural material graphs 1) from image prompts, 2) from text prompts, 3) unconditionally and 4) conditioned on partial graphs (AutoCompletion). The conditioning uses a CLIP-based encoder, according to one summary of the abstract (a multi-modal node graph generation neural architecture for high-quality procedural material synthesis which can be conditioned on different inputs (text or image prompts), using a CLIP-based encoder.).\n\nThe paper positions itself against earlier work. The authors note that the previous approach (MatFormer) was limited to unconditional generation of random node graphs, making the generation of an envisioned material challenging.\n\nSources:\n- arXiv abstract page: https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.13172\n- arXiv PDF: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.13172\n- SIGGRAPH 2023 DOI: https://doi.org/10.1145/3588432.3591520\n\nNote that the SIGGRAPH history archive spells the author's surname \"Hasan,\" while arXiv and the paper itself use \"Hašan.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"426bf26a-5a8e-4a60-beda-bf5d2e315864","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:22:54.328Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bc9a8558-726f-4c15-9fd4-1596cd2b8eef","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f4819cd4-501f-4e63-9268-f4bb9e840842","permission