{"parentUuid":"02ebf15f-95e7-4b40-93e3-15bc01dbd8b4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MHipDBgirXuW3WChUZFon3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VLMaterial procedural material generation large vision-language models ICLR 2025 arXiv\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"VLMaterial: Procedural Material Generation with Large Vision-Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/hash/5393eaf0b723278738788520ec54e4b4-Abstract-Conference.html\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] VLMaterial: Procedural Material Generation with Large Vision-Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://themoonlight.io/review/vlmaterial-procedural-material-generation-with-large-vision-language-models\"},{\"title\":\"close this message\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.18623v2\"},{\"title\":\"[Revue de papier] VLMaterial: Procedural Material Generation with Large Vision-Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/fr/review/vlmaterial-procedural-material-generation-with-large-vision-language-models\"},{\"title\":\"[Papierüberprüfung] VLMaterial: Procedural Material Generation with Large Vision-Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/de/review/vlmaterial-procedural-material-generation-with-large-vision-language-models\"},{\"title\":\"[Revisión de artículo] VLMaterial: Procedural Material Generation with Large Vision-Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/es/review/vlmaterial-procedural-material-generation-with-large-vision-language-models\"},{\"title\":\"people.csail.mit.edu\",\"url\":\"https://people.csail.mit.edu/beichen/publications\"},{\"title\":\"iclr.cc\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/virtual/2025/poster/27856\"},{\"title\":\"iclr.cc\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/media/iclr-2026/Slides/10009540.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VLMaterial: Procedural Material Generation with Large Vision-Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://mlanthology.org/iclr/2025/li2025iclr-vlmaterial\"}]\n\nThe VLMaterial paper was accepted at ICLR 2025 and is also on arXiv as 2501.18623.\n\n**Core idea:** The authors convert procedural materials into standard Python programs, then fine-tune a pre-trained vision-language model to write those programs from an input image. They use this conversion to fine-tune a large pre-trained vision-language model to generate such programs from input images. Their stated motivation is that creating a procedural material from an input image takes professional knowledge and significant effort.\n\n**Contributions:** The team also released data and an augmentation method. They contribute an open-source procedural material dataset and perform program-level augmentation by prompting another pre-trained large language model. According to the abstract, the method outperforms previous methods on both synthetic and real-world examples.\n\n**Publication details:**\n- Authors: Beichen Li, Rundi Wu, Armando Solar-Lezama, Changxi Zheng, Liang Shi, Bernd Bickel, and Wojciech Matusik.\n- arXiv: 2501.18623. The listing shows it was submitted on 27 Jan 2025 (v1), last revised 18 Feb 2025 (this version, v2).\n- ICLR 2025 poster page: iclr.cc/virtual/2025/poster/27856. The proceedings version is also available on the ICLR site.\n\n**Follow-up work:** A later ICLR 2026 slide deck describes a successor called MULTIMAT, which it presents as a multimodal program synthesis VLM for procedural materials with a visual memory. That deck argues that VLMATERIAL generates materials solely as textual programs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"419a17c7-d454-4574-83a6-dd97b30a4f89","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:23:29.626Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c9a435fe-059d-4305-a566-bafa0f55b212","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_b