{"parentUuid":"96a5edf0-62f0-45be-b1a0-c78ed6050579","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vutdj41KYA26e4unDZxEf3","type":"tool_result","content":"**Summary (based only on the README)**\n\n- **Method:** The README says the RL component fine-tunes a conditional MatFormer for node parameter prediction, which generates Substance Designer material graphs conditioned on an input image. It names PPO as the algorithm, since the training scripts and configs are called `train_ppo`. It does not describe the policy architecture in detail.\n- **Reward and similarity metric:** The README does not define the reward function. It mentions an \"image-space metric calculation\" at inference and a `metric_batch_size` setting for \"calculating image simlarities,\" but it does not say which metric is used in training. LPIPS and CLIP appear among the install dependencies, but the README doesn't say how they're used.\n- **Training stages:**\n  1. Supervised pre-training of the parameter generator.\n  2. RL fine-tuning with PPO, in one of two variants: synthetic images only, or a mix of synthetic and real images.\n- **Data:** The paper's dataset and pre-trained model can't be released. The authors plan to release weights for a sample model trained on published materials from DiffMat, \"Please stay tuned for further updates.\"\n- **Inference:** A single script runs parameter prediction, material rendering, image-space metric calculation, and differentiable post-optimization, on synthetic or real test images.\n- **Results:** The README reports no quantitative results and points to the SIGGRAPH Asia 2024 paper. It only describes the output folder structure, which includes side-by-side visual comparison figures."}]},"uuid":"0f1a54e0-277c-460a-b38e-4fff15cbad76","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:17.843Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ae7ac167-f704-4742-879b-