{"parentUuid":"61a105cb-b60f-4e90-a767-a9c3fadb76c6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K7VCmJM2CjSUSzi7pU726T","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\" Hu Hašan Guerrero Rushmeier Deschaintre EGSR 2022\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"controlling material appearance by examples\",\"url\":\"https://research.adobe.com/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/items/056d5968-bc05-4534-bf43-ea91428949a0/full\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14591\"},{\"title\":\"Valentin Deschaintre\",\"url\":\"https://research.adobe.com/person/valentin-deschaintre/\"},{\"title\":\"par.nsf.gov\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/search/author:%22Hu,%20Yiwei%22\"},{\"title\":\"dblp.org\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/224/0692\"},{\"title\":\"@milos hasan\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/@milos-hasan\"},{\"title\":\"dblp.org\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/pid/13/6571\"},{\"title\":\"Miloš Hašan\",\"url\":\"https://backiee.wasmer.app/http_miloshasan_net\"}]\n\nThe paper is by Yiwei Hu, Miloš Hašan, Paul Guerrero, Holly Rushmeier, and Valentin Deschaintre. It was published in Computer Graphics Forum 41(4): 117-128 (2022), and it was presented at EGSR 2022. The DOI is 10.1111/cgf14591.\n\nThe paper proposes an example-based way to edit material maps. Given a user's photos of target materials, the method adjusts an existing material map so that it takes on the target's surface texture. It works by training a tileable version of MaterialGAN and using its learned material prior to steer the appearance transfer. The latent space is optimized through differentiable rendering. The authors say the approach can make existing materials look more realistic or generate new materials.\n\nSources: the Eurographics Association and John Wiley & Sons Ltd. record on the Eurographics Digital Library, and the Adobe Research publication page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b4f5cdfc-c673-4a11-ab26-92955aa811c5","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:29.745Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5b31a403-72fc-4296-87ca-2a3975035c14","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"61a105cb-b60f-4e90-a767-a9c3fadb76c6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"df8f5adf-4f65-460a-9142-fd447c4f7e6e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BfK1GAZBezkYiUPFG3hF3k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\" Guehl Allègre Dischler Benes Galin 2020\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://diglib7.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061\"},{\"title\":\"dc.contributor.author | Guehl, Pascal | en_US |\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061?show=full\"},{\"title\":\"Jean-Michel DISCHLER\",\"url\":\"https://dpt-info.u-strasbg.fr/~dischler\"},{\"title\":\"v39i4pp159 171\",\"url\":\"https://diglib7.eg.org/bitstream/handle/10.1111/cgf14061/v39i4pp159-171.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://cs.purdue.edu/cgvlab/www/publications/Guehl20EGSR\"},{\"title\":\"Jean-Michel DISCHLER\",\"url\":\"https://dpt-info.di.unistra.fr/~dischler/\"},{\"title\":\"r%C3%A9mi all%C3%A8gre\",\"url\":\"https://projet.liris.cnrs.fr/origami/authors/r%C3%A9mi-all%C3%A8gre\"},{\"title\":\"pascal guehl\",\"url\":\"https://projet.liris.cnrs.fr/origami/authors/pascal-guehl/\"},{\"title\":\"1ccf1745 74b1 43d3 8987 64f219583e3f\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/signposting/describedby/1ccf1745-74b1-43d3-8987-64f219583e3f\"}]\n\nThe paper is in *Computer Graphics Forum*, vol. 39, no. 4 (2020), pp. 159–171, presented at the Eurographics Symposium on Rendering 2020. The DOI is 10.1111/cgf.14061, and the authors' Purdue page notes an Honorable mention from the Best Papers Committee.\n\nThe authors are affiliated with ICube, Université de Strasbourg, CNRS, France; Purdue University, USA; and LIRIS, Université de Lyon, CNRS, France.\n\n**Approach (from the abstract):** The paper proposes a hybrid method for generating textures. Its pipeline separates structure from color. Structure comes from a parametric model, and color comes from exemplar data. The core component is a Point Process Texture Basis Function (PPTBF), which the abstract describes as extending sparse convolution noises by defining rich convolution kernels. Those kernels pair a window function with a correlated statistical mixture of Gabor functions, meant to cover patterns such as cells, cracks, grains, and waves.\n\n**Key properties:**\n- Parameters can be set automatically from binary structure exemplars.\n- Because the model relies on one parameter set, it supports continuous transitions between different visual structures.\n- Color is handled by a multiscale parallel texture synthesis by numbers, constrained by the PPTBF.\n- The authors state that the resulting textures are parametric, infinite and avoid repetition.\n\nIf you need the full text, the DOI link and the PDF on the Eurographics digital library are the primary sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"b7d0e989-cda0-4cd6-a7be-876099e2157f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:32.510Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5b31a403-72fc-4296-87ca-2a3975035c14","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"df8f5adf-4f65-460a-9142-fd447c4f7e6e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":