{"parentUuid":"195fa7b3-9dec-490b-a822-18073133322e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AsLxzxRpe2HGXboZb7x6tk","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Hu \"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\" arXiv tileable MaterialGAN guidance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"@yiwei hu\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/@yiwei-hu\"},{\"title\":\"controlling material appearance by examples\",\"url\":\"https://research.adobe.com/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples\"},{\"title\":\"@milos hasan\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/@milos-hasan\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://deepai.org/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/items/056d5968-bc05-4534-bf43-ea91428949a0/full\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://api.deepai.org/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14591\"},{\"title\":\"controlling material appearance by examples\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples/\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling Material Appearance by Examples\",\"url\":\"https://cdnjs.deepai.org/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples\"},{\"title\":\"056d5968 bc05 4534 bf43 ea91428949a0\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/signposting/describedby/056d5968-bc05-4534-bf43-ea91428949a0\"}]\n\nI couldn't find an arXiv listing in these results, but the paper is indexed under several other sources. It was published in Computer Graphics Forum (EGSR 2022). The authors are Yiwei Hu, Miloš Hašan, Paul Guerrero, Holly Rushmeier, and Valentin Deschaintre. The DOI is 10.1111/cgf.14591, and it appears in volume 41, issue 4, pages 117–128 ([diglib.eg.org](https://diglib.eg.org/items/056d5968-bc05-4534-bf43-ea91428949a0/full)).\n\n**The method:** The paper proposes an example-based way to edit existing material maps using photos supplied by the user. It trains a tileable MaterialGAN and uses that model's learned material prior to steer the appearance transfer. The latent space is optimized through differentiable rendering ([research.adobe.com](https://research.adobe.com/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples)).\n\n**What it preserves:** According to the abstract, the approach carries over fine micro- and meso-scale texture from the target photos while keeping the input's structure and material quality ([diglib.eg.org](https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14591)). The PapersCopilot summary adds that the output keeps the input's tileability ([papercopilot.com](https://papercopilot.com/paper/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples/)).\n\n**Use cases:** The authors say the method can refine existing materials for realism or generate new materials ([deepai.org](https://deepai.org/publication/controlling-material-appearance-by-examples)). It can also transfer appearance from several targets with region-level control, according to the PapersCopilot listing.\n\nIf you need the arXiv version specifically, search arXiv directly for the title. The DOI above will also resolve to the published version.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7d55dbe4-cdda-42dd-a7e2-80d055bd9801","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:24:57.350Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d8ca09a0-d10c-47b1-96e9-aac7c3d53cbf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"195