{"parentUuid":"7adf48a6-aa3c-42ec-bf41-a8aace462cea","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U6tDyR3M5CjrW7bLUFgkvp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PPTBF semi-procedural textures github ASTex parameter estimation binary structure CNN database Guehl\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://diglib7.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://diglib7.eg.org/items/1ccf1745-74b1-43d3-8987-64f219583e3f/full\"},{\"title\":\"1ccf1745 74b1 43d3 8987 64f219583e3f\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/signposting/describedby/1ccf1745-74b1-43d3-8987-64f219583e3f\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/items/1ccf1745-74b1-43d3-8987-64f219583e3f/full\"},{\"title\":\"v39i4pp159 171\",\"url\":\"https://diglib7.eg.org/bitstream/handle/10.1111/cgf14061/v39i4pp159-171.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"dc.contributor.author | Guehl, Pascal | en_US |\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061?show=full\"},{\"title\":\"Webpage : https://egsr2020.london/\",\"url\":\"https://publis.icube.unistra.fr/4-GADB20\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-03083276\"},{\"title\":\"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\",\"url\":\"https://cs.purdue.edu/cgvlab/www/publications/Guehl20EGSR\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the paper behind the PPTBF approach, but nothing about a GitHub repository, an ASTex connection, or a CNN-based database, so those parts of your query remain unverified.\n\n**The paper:** \"Semi-Procedural Textures Using Point Process Texture Basis Functions\" by P. Guehl, R. Allègre, J.-M. Dischler, B. Benes, and E. Galin, published in Computer Graphics Forum (2020, vol. 39, no. 4, pp. 159–171, DOI 10.1111/cgf.14061). It was presented at the Eurographics Symposium on Rendering 2020 and received an honorable mention from the Best Papers Committee. ([Purdue](https://cs.purdue.edu/cgvlab/www/publications/Guehl20EGSR), [Eurographics DL](https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061))\n\n**What the method does:**\n- It splits synthesis into two stages: a procedural structure stage and a data-driven color stage. ([Eurographics DL](https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061))\n- The PPTBF extends sparse convolution noise with richer kernels, combining a window function with a correlated mixture of Gabor functions. These are meant to cover structures such as cells, cracks, grains, scratches, spots, stains, and waves. ([Eurographics DL](https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061))\n- Its parameters can be estimated automatically from binary structure exemplars. ([Eurographics DL](https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061))\n- Color is synthesized from the exemplar with a multiscale parallel texture synthesis by numbers, constrained by the PPTBF. ([Eurographics DL](https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.1111/cgf14061))\n- The paper describes parameters being estimated from an input, edited by hand, or explored through database browsing and latent appearance space inspection. ([Eurographics PDF](https://diglib7.eg.org/bitstream/handle/10.1111/cgf14061/v39i4pp159-171.pdf))\n\n**Not found in results:**\n- **GitHub code:** No repository or code release appeared. The paper's author page and the Purdue listing are the closest official pages.\n- **ASTex:** No reference to ASTex (the Strasbourg-based texture analysis group) appeared, though the authors are affiliated with ICube at the Université de Strasbourg.\n- **CNN database:** The search did not show a CNN-based texture database or a link between CNNs and this method. The paper's database-browsing feature is the only related item I found.\n\nIf you need code or the database component, a search on the authors' lab pages or the paper's supplementary material would be the next step.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e23e284a-1924-4f59-8e8e-5f7b07599df2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:10.022Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d07ead2f-3672-46db-a76a-2061473faf72","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7adf48a6-aa3c-42ec-bf41-a8aace462cea","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
