{"parentUuid":"1c39e2e1-42e2-49f2-9891-5f63993180d8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RbWv6ef1XBS3nfxB6jPDYZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Substance 3D Sampler Image to Material AI powered height normal generation documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"height to normal\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/tools/height-to-normal.html\"},{\"title\":\"version 4 2\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/release-notes/version-4-2.html\"},{\"title\":\"image to material\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/tools/image-to-material.html\"},{\"title\":\"version 2020 2 2 2\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/release-notes/old-versions/version-2020-2-2-2.html\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide Cancel\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/tools/normal-to-height.html\"},{\"title\":\"Image To Material\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-sampler/using/filters/tools/image-to-material\"},{\"title\":\"keyshot 9\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/getting-started/export/default-presets/keyshot-9.html\"},{\"title\":\"Version 4.2\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-sampler/using/release-notes/version-4-2\"},{\"title\":\"delight ai powered\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/filters/tools/delight-ai-powered.html\"},{\"title\":\"version 3 3\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-sampler/release-notes/version-3-3.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up Adobe's documentation for the AI-powered Image to Material filter, which covers height and normal generation. The dedicated Height to Normal page returned only navigation text, so I couldn't confirm its contents.\n\n**Image to Material (AI Powered)**\n- The current docs on Experience League describe Image to Material as a template for building a PBR material from one input photo. It offers two algorithms: AI Powered and B2M.\n- The AI Powered option relies on machine learning to identify shapes and objects, which lets it produce height and normal maps. It also works to strip shadows and highlights out of the base color. (The AI Powered algorithm uses machine learning to recognize shapes and objects and accurately generate, Normal, Height and Roughness maps.)\n- Training covered a broad range of surfaces, like fabrics, organics, indoors and outdoor surfaces.\n- Performance is a practical caveat: the AI route is slower on large images, so the docs suggest managing the Layer Resolution system to optimize your workflow while working.\n- The B2M algorithm is the non-AI alternative. It may produce less accurate results but will work on a wider range of input images.\n\n**Version history**\n- The AI approach first appeared in Substance Alchemist 2020.2. At that point, the docs said it uses machine learning to recognize shapes and objects and accurately generate height and normal information.\n- Sampler 4.2 (September 2023) introduced an updated AI version. Its docs say the updated version of Image to Material improves the material generation and the range of materials supported. Now, Image to Material has been trained on all material types. It also added a parameter for choosing the material type.\n\n**Related filters**\n- A separate AI Upscale filter enhances base color, normal, height, roughness, and metallic channels of your material.\n- The Normal to Height filter has its own page on HelpX, but its body text didn't come through in the results. Check the Experience League version directly for its details.\n\nNote that many HelpX pages now redirect to Experience League, so use the Experience League links when you want the current documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2373ec5a-6fa5-4ed0-be66-11898f7a051a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:27.442Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f6aa2cf8-1569-45ab-a258-7c22a56521fd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1c39e2e1-42e2-49f2-9891-5f63993180d8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8a5a3b5a-554d-4c1d-bdab-68a3b17c47c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0143wH2HK7Z8xsGdWrKqtUyL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ArmorLab AI texture generation photo to PBR material height map armory3d\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Create Your\",\"url\":\"https://armory3d.org/lab\"},{\"title\":\"Version 0.1\",\"url\":\"https://armory3d.org/lab/manual\"},{\"title\":\"A downloadable tool for Windows, macOS, and Linux\",\"url\":\"https://armory.itch.io/armorlab\"},{\"title\":\"ArmorPaint & ArmorLab - Le Bottin des Jeux Linux\",\"url\":\"https://lebottinlinux.vps.a-lec.org/Bottin_0-C_files/ArmorPaint___ArmorLab-16293.html\"},{\"title\":\"Build Games in Blender\",\"url\":\"https://armory3d.org\"},{\"title\":\"aichief.com\",\"url\":\"https://aichief.com/alternatives/armorlab/\"},{\"title\":\"5 Best AI Texture & Material Generators in 2026: PBR, Seamless & Game-Ready Assets\",\"url\":\"https://www.lovart.ai/it/blog/5-best-ai-texture-material-generators-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Best AI Texture and PBR Material Generators in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.3daistudio.com/blog/best-ai-texture-and-pbr-generators-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Friday, September 4th, 2026 Posted by Jim Thacker\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgchannel.com/?p=178507\"},{\"title\":\"ArmorLab logo\",\"url\":\"https://neura.market/ai-tools-directory/3d-model-generators/armorlab\"}]\n\nArmorLab is a separate desktop app from the Armory3D game engine, made by the same team. It can turn a photo into a PBR material set that includes a height map.\n\n**What it does**\n- The official ArmorLab page says it can extract base color, height, normal map, occlusion and roughness textures from a photo using a pre-trained deep neural network. It also supports creating seamless PBR materials using text prompts.\n- Other tools include a tiling node, an upscale node, a text-guided variance node, and an inpaint node for filling in texture details or removing unwanted parts from a photo by painting a mask.\n\n**Relation to Armory3D**\n- The Armory3D site lists ArmorLab as a stand-alone software designed for AI-powered texture authoring. ArmorPaint is the sibling painting tool, and Blender, Unreal Engine and Unity plugin previews are available for download. I found no evidence that ArmorLab is an Armory3D or Blender add-on, so you would export its maps and import them into armory3d yourself.\n- A recent release note says ArmorPaint 1.0 includes AI-based image upscaling and photo-to-material generation. If you want that workflow inside the Armory ecosystem, check whether ArmorPaint 1.0 covers your needs before buying ArmorLab.\n\n**Platform and cost**\n- The itch.io listing shows Windows, Linux (cpu only) and macOS (apple silicon) builds, a minimum price of $19, and a refund policy.\n- The manual recommends GTX 1060/6GB or better and notes that processing time depends on a graphics card performance.\n- The manual also says the preview version has many rough edges and the experience may be frustrating.\n\n**Conflicting claims**\nThird-party directories disagree with the official listing. One calls ArmorLab a free, open-source desktop application, but the paid itch.io page and the Linux directory's description of ArmorPaint as libre don't support that. Another says it is priced from just $19, which matches the official listing. I'd rely on the armory3d.org pages and the itch.io listing for licensing and feature details, and check the current build and version on the official site.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6221fc76-c08f-4a2e-809a-8cec5827fd8a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:29.009Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f6aa2cf8-1569-45ab-a258-7c22a56521fd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":nu