anji Shader\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/r21/us/html/XSLABANJI-ID_BANJI_DIFFUSE.html\"},{\"title\":\"normal to height filter output luminosity changes depending on resolution 630293\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/questions-69/normal-to-height-filter-output-luminosity-changes-depending-on-resolution-630293\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Features Material Manager Extensions Volumetric Shaders Nukei Shader\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/r21/us/html/XSLANUKEI-ID_NUKEI_DIFFUSE_B.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Features Material Manager Extensions Volumetric Shaders Banji Shader\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/s22/us/html/XSLABANJI-ID_BANJI_DIFFUSE.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Features Material Manager Extensions Volumetric Shaders Nukei Shader\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/r21/us/html/XSLANUKEI-ID_NUKEI_DIFFUSE_A.html\"},{\"title\":\"Diffuse Level\",\"url\":\"https://download.autodesk.com/us/3DSmax/2012help/files/GUID-A5230575-7258-45FE-81C4-234F40F86A3-1987.htm\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Features Material Manager Extensions Volumetric Shaders Mabel Shader\",\"url\":\"https://help.maxon.net/c4d/s22/us/html/XSLAMABEL-ID_MABEL_DIFFUSE_A.html\"}]\n\nI couldn't find a source that explains the internal algorithm behind Materialize's diffuse-to-height conversion. The search results confirm that the feature exists and how to use it at a high level.\n\n**What the sources confirm**\n\n- Materialize is a free, GPL-licensed tool from Bounding Box Software that turns photos into PBR materials. Bounding Box Software – aka game developer Mike Voeller – has developed Materialize, a free tool that converts photographs into PBR materials.\n- Diffuse-to-height is one of its supported conversions. The Valve Developer Wiki says it also can create Heightmaps and Bump maps from a Diffuse texture. Its list of supported transitions includes Diffuse→Heightmap.\n- Adjustment is done with sliders. Digital Production notes that with the help of sliders for converting the individual maps and the PBR material, finer adjustments can also be made.\n- Height can then feed other maps. Other supported conversions include Heightmap→Normal Map, and Height + Diffuse -> Normal.\n\n**What's missing**\n\n- The Valve wiki's step-by-step guide cuts off right at the section on creating a map from a diffuse texture, so the specific procedure isn't visible in the results.\n- None of the sources explain what image property the height is derived from or what each slider does.\n\n**General context (not from these sources)**\n\nTools in this category typically estimate height from the diffuse image's brightness or luminance, then use contrast and level-style sliders to control the result. Materialize may work this way, but I haven't verified it. To confirm, check the tool's documentation on GitHub (the source is at github.com/BoundingBoxSoftware/Materialize, per ToolFarm) or the Valve wiki page for the full guide.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6c4f2024-58d8-42f1-a320-f98197a08e95","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:29.759Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f6aa2cf8-1569-45ab-a258-7c22a56521fd","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2f070cbc-576f-492d-9735-ff84a1b121de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
