{"parentUuid":"df974afb-e31c-4003-a481-75b399a21943","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C5BJy44eQhfja1snRQN5z4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Houdini Neural Layer to Depth MoGe-2 COP node documentation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Neural Layer to Depth (MoGe-2) COP\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/ml/neural_nodes/inference_images.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/subnet.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/convertdepth.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/layertogeo.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/edgedetectdepth.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/output.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/input.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/fetch.html\"},{\"title\":\"On this page |\",\"url\":\"https://sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/index.html\"}]\n\nThe SideFX documentation has a page for this node, titled \"Neural Layer to Depth (MoGe-2) COP.\" It sits in the machine learning section under neural nodes, at sidefx.com/docs/houdini/ml/neural_nodes/inference_images.html. It estimates scene information from an input image using Microsoft's MoGe-2 model. The model produces several outputs: a metric-scale depth map, normal map, and position map, along with a sky mask and a 3D point cloud of the visible image surfaces.\n\nThe same page also documents the neighboring Neural Layer to Mask (SAM2) COP, which creates an image segmentation mask based on prompts using Meta's SAM 2 model.\n\nThe search didn't return the node's parameter list, inputs, or outputs, so for those details, open the linked page directly. The results also included Japanese-language SideFX pages for related COP nodes, such as Convert Depth, which is a Houdini 21.0 node that converts Depth layers into height, depth, and distance. That node may be useful if you want to post-process the depth output.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d82072b0-a247-4bd5-beed-87a24bcfcaf6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:40.302Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"597e7e4a-82a7-4558-a67b-5d10cc480517","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"df974afb-e31c-4003-a481-75b399a21943","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"9f3e28bd-a13d-42dd-9a22-58574a6b5cb4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011aF9eU2CrcN78qmxHCqrFK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MoGe-2 accurate monocular geometry metric scale sharp details arXiv 2025 normal map\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MoGe-2: Accurate Monocular Geometry with Metric Scale and Sharp Details\",\"url\":\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/?p=1153778\"},{\"title\":\"MoGe-2: Accurate Monocular Geometry with Metric Scale and Sharp Details\",\"url\":\"https://nips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/120258\"},{\"title\":\"MoGe-2: Accurate Monocular Geometry with Metric Scale and Sharp Details\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/virtual/2025/poster/120258\"},{\"title\":\"MoGe-2: Accurate Monocular Geometry with Metric Scale and Sharp Details\",\"url\":\"https://papers.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2025/hash/336572db3e99930814d6b328d4220cb6-Abstract-Conference.html\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.02546v1\"},{\"title\":\"Submission #19\",\"url\":\"https://zedd.cs.princeton.edu/submission/19/\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CNES/MoGe\"},{\"title\":\"gitee.com\",\"url\":\"https://gitee.com/minttang/MoGe\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/microsoft/moge\"},{\"title\":\"MoGe-2: Accurate Monocular Geometry with Metric Scale and Sharp Details\",\"url\":\"https://mlanthology.org/neurips/2025/wang2025neurips-moge2\"}]\n\nMoGe-2 is a 2025 paper from Ruicheng Wang and colleagues, accepted to NeurIPS 2025 and posted to arXiv as 2507.02546. The arXiv record shows a July 3, 2025 submission date.\n\n**What it does:** The model estimates a metric-scale 3D point map from one image. It builds on MoGe, which predicts affine-invariant point maps with unknown scales. The authors explore ways to extend MoGe to metric geometry prediction without sacrificing the relative geometry accuracy of the affine-invariant representation.\n\n**Sharp details:** The authors found that noise and errors in real training data wash out fine-grained detail in predicted geometry. Their fix is a data refinement step that filters and completes real data using sharp synthetic labels, which improves the granularity of the reconstructed geometry while keeping overall accuracy.\n\n**Normal maps:** The official MoGe GitHub README lists MoGe-2's new capabilities as point map prediction in metric scale, comparable or better performance than MoGe-1, significant improvement of visual sharpness, high-quality normal map estimation, and lower inference latency. The repo also notes that normal maps are one of the outputs, alongside metric depth and camera FOV.\n\n**Where to look:** The arXiv abstract is at arxiv.org/abs/2507.02546, the project page is wangrc.site/MoGe2Page, and code is in the microsoft/MoGe repository. The search results did not include the paper's own normal-map benchmark numbers, so check the full PDF if you need those.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8522aedd-267c-4b17-822c-ddd3b279c4d8","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:25:41.379Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"597e7e4a-82a7-4558-a67b-5d10cc480517","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f3e28bd-a13d-42dd-9a22-58574a6b5cb4","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
