{"parentUuid":"5c7c71b4-3ede-41d0-939a-9cf811e45ebf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HYFCoGQQViVy2Vrfc4xrvg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Gabor noise by example\" Galerne Lagae Lefebvre Drettakis SIGGRAPH 2012 power spectrum estimation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"“Gabor noise by example” by Galerne, Lagae, Lefebvre and Drettakis – ACM SIGGRAPH HISTORY ARCHIVES\",\"url\":\"https://history.siggraph.org/?p=110552\"},{\"title\":\"Gabor Noise by Example\",\"url\":\"https://hal-univ-tlse3.archives-ouvertes.fr/INRIA/hal-00695670\"},{\"title\":\"history.siggraph.org\",\"url\":\"https://history.siggraph.org/?p=209922\"},{\"title\":\"Procedural noise using sparse Gabor convolution\",\"url\":\"https://www.academia.edu/2854650/Procedural_noise_using_sparse_Gabor_convolution\"},{\"title\":\"class gabor noise\",\"url\":\"https://perso.liris.cnrs.fr/eric.galin/Doc/Core/class_gabor_noise.html\"},{\"title\":\"LD11FSGN supplementary\",\"url\":\"https://graphics.cs.kuleuven.be/publications/LD11FSGN/LD11FSGN_supplementary.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"“Filtering solid Gabor noise” by Lagae and Drettakis – ACM SIGGRAPH HISTORY ARCHIVES\",\"url\":\"https://history.siggraph.org/?p=114638\"},{\"title\":\"charpenay 2014 sgn paper.pdf\",\"url\":\"https://www.cg.tuwien.ac.at/research/publications/2014/charpenay-2014-sgn/charpenay-2014-sgn-paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"BLVLDT10 sketch\",\"url\":\"https://artis.inrialpes.fr/Publications/2010/BLVLDT10a/BLVLDT10_sketch.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the paper's abstract, its publication details, and some context from later papers.\n\n**What the paper does:** It estimates the parameters of bandwidth-quantized Gabor noise, a procedural noise function that can generate noise with an arbitrary power spectrum, from exemplar Gaussian textures, which are fully characterized by their power spectrum. The authors' estimation step automatically decomposes the noisy power spectrum estimate of an exemplar into a sparse sum of Gaussians using non-negative basis pursuit denoising. The method also includes an efficient procedural evaluation scheme that uses multi-grid evaluation and importance sampling of the kernel parameters.\n\n**Publication details:** The SIGGRAPH archive lists it under the authors Galerne, Lagae, Lefebvre and Drettakis. A reference in the SIGGRAPH archive gives the venue as ACM Trans. Graph. 31, 4 (July), 73:1–73:9. The search results don't state the 2012 conference year directly. A later paper, though, cites the work as Galerne et al. 2012, which presents a generalized noise process that aims at the reconstruction of Gabor functions from example textures.\n\n**Context:** A later paper says most of the work on Gabor noise is due to Ares Lagae and co-workers. It describes the earlier work as follows: the original concept of Gabor noise bringing together the Gabor kernel function, and the sparse convolution evaluation (random pulse process) came from Lagae et al. 2009, Lagae, S. Lefebvre, G. Drettakis, and P. Dutré, 2009. Procedural noise using sparse Gabor convolution. ACM Trans. Graph. 28, 3, 54:1–54:10.\n\nA project page is listed in the HAL archive: http://graphics.cs.kuleuven.be/publications/GLLD12GNBE/. I didn't open it, so I can't confirm its contents.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"96e5dd6b-f883-48df-8e9d-9f34b6cc0072","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:04.653Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"05001b92-fac9-441b-8c1c-7d0e1a480149","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5c7c71b4-3ede-41d0-939a-9cf811e45ebf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"