{"parentUuid":"6d7d8a1f-ce2c-48d4-bfad-f465e2df8170","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QsmBCXneUr7UjHjQxsUbF4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Portilla Simoncelli 2000 \"A Parametric Texture Model Based on Joint Statistics of Complex Wavelet Coefficients\" statistics list\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Parametric Texture Model based on Joint Statistics of Complex Wavelet Coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://www.cns.nyu.edu/~eero/ABSTRACTS/portilla99-abstract.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.cns.nyu.edu\",\"url\":\"https://www.cns.nyu.edu/pub/eero/portilla99.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"portilla99 reprint\",\"url\":\"https://www.cns.nyu.edu/pub/eero/portilla99-reprint.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"A Parametric Texture Model Based on Joint Statistics of Complex Wavelet Coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://datalearner.com/academic/journal-papers/0920-5691/volumes-and-issues/40/paper-detail/12867\"},{\"title\":\"Texture Characterization via Joint Statistics of Wavelet Coefficient Magnitudes\",\"url\":\"https://www.cns.nyu.edu/~eero/ABSTRACTS/simoncelli98b-abstract.html\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/LabForComputationalVision/textureSynth\"},{\"title\":\"Texture Modeling and Synthesis using Joint Statistics of Complex Wavelet Coefficients\",\"url\":\"https://www.cns.nyu.edu/~eero/ABSTRACTS/portilla99a-abstract.html\"},{\"title\":\"nyu.edu\",\"url\":\"https://www.cns.nyu.edu/pub/eero/simoncelli98b.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ordb.biotech.ttu.edu\",\"url\":\"https://ordb.biotech.ttu.edu/ORModelDB/Data/109143\"},{\"title\":\"itts023d.itts.ttu.edu\",\"url\":\"https://itts023d.itts.ttu.edu/ORModelDB/Data/109143\"}]\n\nI couldn't find a complete enumerated list of the statistics in the search results, but they describe the model's main components.\n\n- **Pairwise coefficient statistics:** The model is built from statistics computed on pairs of coefficients at adjacent spatial locations, orientations, and scales.\n- **Correlation and magnitude products:** The authors measure the expected product of the raw coefficient pairs (i.e., correlation), and the expected product of their magnitudes.\n- **Cross-scale phase term:** For adjacent scales, they also include the expected product of the fine scale coefficient with the phase-doubled coarse scale coefficient.\n- **Summary from the workshop version:** A related 1999 abstract describes the characterization as parameterized by (1) the local auto-correlation of the coefficients in each subband; (2) both the local auto-correlation and cross-correlation of coefficient magnitudes at other orientations and spatial scales; and (3) the first few moments of the image pixel histogram.\n\nFor the exact full list with counts and definitions, check the paper itself. The reprint is at https://www.cns.nyu.edu/pub/eero/portilla99-reprint.pdf. The actively-maintained GPU-compatible python port of this model (using pytorch) can be found in the plenoptic package. Its documentation notes that it returns only the statistics described in the paper (this implementation includes some redundant statistics, see plenoptic docs for more details).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0f1c8905-08ec-468e-b0ca-e8c4d26c0a1b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:05.262Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"05001b92-fac9-441b-8c1c-7d0e1a480149","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d7d8a1f-ce2c-48d4-bfad-f465e2df8170","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1"