{"parentUuid":"c84c2137-10c0-4619-91dd-28e58d1f72c9","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DbfDhQt9efdFqrqHrDPfVL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Houdini 22 Copernicus new features what's new COPs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Watch Houdini 22 Keynote & Explore New Features\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/everything-you-need-to-know-about-houdini-22\"},{\"title\":\"First Look At New Features In Houdini 22\",\"url\":\"https://80.lv/articles/get-a-first-look-at-houdini-22\"},{\"title\":\"H22 Launch and HIVE\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/houdini-hive/h22-launch-and-hive/\"},{\"title\":\"Sneak peek: Houdini 22\",\"url\":\"https://www.cgchannel.com/2026/06/sneak-peek-houdini-22/\"},{\"title\":\"H22\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/learn/talks/whats-new-in-copernicus/\"},{\"title\":\"H22 World Building\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/products/whats-new-in-h22/world-building/\"},{\"title\":\"What’s new Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/22/copernicus.html\"},{\"title\":\"Here comes Houdini 22\",\"url\":\"https://digitalproduction.com/2026/06/23/here-comes-houdini-22/\"},{\"title\":\"Cops - Houdini and CG tips\",\"url\":\"https://www.tokeru.com/cgwiki/HoudiniCops.html\"}]\n\nHoudini 22's biggest Copernicus (COPs) changes center on terrain, texturing, baking, and VFX. The most concrete details come from SideFX's own pages and the launch coverage.\n\n**Terrain moves into COPs**\nHoudini 22 moves height field work out of SOPs and into Copernicus. A significant architectural shift takes place in terrains, since all heightfield workflows have been migrated from SOPs into COPs. SideFX says this brings faster performance, new terrain tools, integrated machine learning, and streamlined visualization. A new Height Field Strata node adds layered rock detail to terrains, with included recipes combining strata and slump for realistic sedimentary effects. The terrain session also introduces a \"two-flag\" workflow for previewing 3D height and texture at once, plus the Strata and Clip nodes and a revamped color ramp preset system.\n\n**Texturing and node library**\nThe release adds a large batch of nodes. One SideFX talk notes Houdini 22's massive update of 123 new COP nodes. Highlights include nine versatile new grunge maps and the Weave and Knit generators that output custom IDs and UVs. The Mask Combine node lets you bundle several baked maps into one cable for masking. Earlier pattern tools mentioned in the sneak peek include a UV Shape node to Neural Cellular Automata.\n\n**Baking**\nThe new Bake Pre-Process node features interactive viewport tools—including split UV seams to prevent skewing and clear intersection highlighting, which helps you adjust the cage and ray offsets before exporting texture maps to engines like Unreal.\n\n**VFX and simulation**\nThe GPU Pyro solver in COPs has been substantially reworked, with a streamlined Pyro block layout and an implicit surface workflow for sourcing. Digital Production reports that the Copernicus-based Sparse GPU Fluid Solver has been upgraded from a simplified background experiment into a full production solver on SOP and DOP level. Implicit surfaces are generated on the GPU and immediately used there as efficient collision objects or source geometry for fluid simulation. The sneak peek also showed a 'ripple solver with adjacency maps and time shift'.\n\n**Integration with other areas**\nKarma and Solaris can now work with COPs more directly. Solaris gets a Texture Material Library LOP that allows a tight loop for COP-based texturing directly in combination with Karma. Karma also gains live COP texturing viewports. Houdini 22 also includes \"direct COP support via HDA in Unreal Engine\", according to the sneak peek coverage.\n\n**Other notes**\nDigital Production says the 2D and 3D painting functions are now fully integrated in this release. The sneak peek also mentions a Rectangular method for the Quad Remesh node, though that is outside COPs.\n\nFor full node-by-node details, check SideFX's \"What's new Copernicus\" docs page, which lists the new nodes and improvements.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d97398f6-0d67-413a-bf48-4b6435c33c1a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:36.439Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"83b0dc63-4a6b-49a8-9ba0-145e602b9ad0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c84c2137-10c0-4619-91dd-28e58d1f72c9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
