context is a 2D and 3D GPU image processing framework that provides real-time image manipulation and is ideal for tasks such as building texture maps and setting up Slap Comps. Use nodes such as Tile Pattern or SDF Shapes to build up texture maps with noise, distortion and the rasterization of 3D shapes.\n- The Triplanar Hex Tile node is documented as a Houdini 21.0 addition (\"Since 21.0\"). Its docs describe it as generating seamless, non-repeating texturing and normal mapping through triplanar projection. The node uses adjacent hexagonal tiles across the X, Y, and Z projections, and randomly scales and rotates tiles for a natural look. Its parameters include Size, Scale, Scale Random, Rotate, Rotate Random, Random Seed, Contrast, Falloff, Weight Exp, and per-axis triplanar controls. This is from the Japanese-language version of the SideFX docs, so the parameter descriptions are my translation.\n- I did not find a dedicated Stamp node page in the results. The Japanese docs page for the Triplanar Hex Tile node has a fragment mentioning copying a stamp and applying a transform to the copy, plus a Corner Pin entry, but it is too fragmentary to confirm what the Stamp node does in 21.0.\n\n**Context**\n- SideFX released Houdini 21 in August 2025. SideFX has released Houdini 21, adding rigging, CFX, VFX, lookdev, terrain, and Copernicus updates. Digital Production also noted that the release notes remain cautious, focusing instead on tool improvements without broad guarantees.\n- Copernicus was introduced in Houdini 20.5. It's a successor to Houdini's old compositing framework, and a much broader toolset, bringing with it new capabilities, including material-authoring workflows reminiscent of Substance 3D Designer.\n- Houdini 21 also added texture baking in Copernicus and in Karma, according to a French summary of the SIGGRAPH keynote. Des solutions de baking de textures sont disponibles à la fois dans Copernicus et dans Karma.\n\nFor exact Tile Pattern and Stamp parameters and the official 21.0 change list, check the Houdini 21.0 Copernicus node pages on sidefx.com (for example, Tile Pattern and Stamp under \"Houdini 21.0 Nodes > Copernicus nodes\") and the Houdini 21 release notes page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d6d84294-994d-43ae-8c58-8e4c0126e07f","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:36.626Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"83b0dc63-4a6b-49a8-9ba0-145e602b9ad0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb5e0379-fb17-4237-bf9c-f82d73fd70c0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
