rypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"864c189a-854e-430f-af7a-7356ee95db89","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiUDATSSsWpr5uRmU3byPu","type":"tool_result","content":"# Copernicus in Houdini 21: Texture and Height Map Building\n\nThe page doesn't mention tile pattern changes, distort-by-slope recipes, statistics nodes, or Substance, so I've left those out.\n\n**Baking and UDIM**\n- Bake Geometry Textures COP: transfers geometry data from one mesh to another.\n- Ray Trace COP: casts rays against incoming geometry and reports the first intersection.\n- UDIM parameter on COP Network, COP Network SOP, the network toolbar, and as a context option: sets a global UDIM that replaces any `<UDIM>` token in filenames.\n- Match UDIM COP: reframes a layer's pixels to fit a specific UDIM tile.\n- File COP: supports `<UDIM>` and `<LAYER>` tokens, plus a UDIM parameter.\n- ROP Image Output COP: supports `<UDIM>`, `<LAYER>`, and `<F>`/`<F#>` tokens, plus a UDIM Range parameter.\n\n**Tiling**\n- Support for 2D tiling in Copernicus.\n- Hyperbolic Tile COP: generates tiles built from hyperbolic regular polygons.\n- Triplanar Hex Tile COP: textures large areas in triplanar projections without visible repetition.\n\n**Triplanar and projection**\n- Triplanar COP: projects X, Y, and Z textures onto a position layer.\n- Triplanar UV COP: generates UVs for X, Y, and Z projections.\n- Triplanar Hex Tile COP (listed above).\n- Position Sample COP: samples an input texture based on position.\n- Space Transform COP: converts position, vector, and UV values between camera spaces.\n- Vector Transform 2D COP: transforms UV values in 2D.\n- Position Map COP: adds a Source Position parameter.\n- Preview Material COP: adds Rotate, Remove Caps, and MikkT Tangent Space parameters.\n\n**Stamping and scatter**\n- Scatter Shapes COP: generates and scatters stamps across an image.\n- Scatter on Curves COP: scatters stamps along a curve.\n- Copy and Transform COP: duplicates an input stamp and transforms the copies.\n- Stash COP: stores the node's inputs for use as output.\n\n**Curves and masks**\n- Curve 3D COP: interactive Bézier curve drawing and editing.\n- Layer from Curves COP: builds a layer from curves.\n- Mask from Curves COP: creates a black-and-white mask from 2D curves.\n- Rasterize Curves COP: rasterizes curves.\n- Bend COP: bends an image using pivot handles or a captured region.\n- Lattice Deform COP: applies grid-based deformation to an image.\n\n**SDF, flood fill, and segmentation**\n- SDF to Mono COP: gains a Shadow Value parameter (existing node).\n- Fill Connected COP: fills connected pixel regions with a constant value.\n- Segment by Connectivity COP: gains a Collapse IDs parameter (existing node).\n\n**Blocks and simulation**\n- Reaction-Diffusion Block Begin COP and Reaction-Diffusion Block End COP: start and end a 2D reaction-diffusion simulation.\n- Flow Block COPs: 2D fluid solver blocks (see the Flow Solver).\n- Block End COP: adds Simulate and Live Simulation parameters for feedback loops.\n- Block to Geometry COP: gains an Input States parameter.\n- Note: Flow Blocks and Pyro require DOP-level permissions, so they're unavailable in Houdini Core.\n\n**Height and depth**\n- Convert Depth COP: converts depth layers to and from depth, distance, and height spaces.\n- HeightField Visualize COP: visualizes layers as colored heightfields.\n- Height to Shadow COP: generates shadows from a virtual light.\n- Heat Distort COP and Heat Distort by Layer COP: heat-haze style distortion.\n- Lens Distort COP: distorts a layer using OpenCV coefficients.\n- Height types now render as heightfields in the Scene View and as hillshades in the Composite View and thumbnails.\n- Geometry to Layer COP: version 2.0, converts 2D and 3D volumes into layers.\n\n**Edges, curvature, and derivatives**\n- Curvature COP: computes the curvature of a layer.\n- Derivative COP: adds Forward and Diagonal Difference Mode options.\n- Edge Detect COP: adds Normalize, removes Details, and renames the Canny method to Thresholded Sobel.\n- Edge Detect by Contour COP, Edge Detect by Depth COP, and Edge Detect by Normal COP: add Edge Spread and remove Line Quality.\n\n**Noise and procedural patterns**\n- Phasor Noise COP: organic wave patterns.\n- Bubble Noise COP: bubbly patterns.\n- Cloud Noise 3D COP: billowy cloud patterns.\n- Crystal Noise COP: sharp, angular Worley-type noise.\n- Chladni Cymatic Patterns COP: interference patterns from two frequencies.\n- Worley Noise COP and Worley Noise 3D COP: gain post-processing parameters.\n- Fractal Noise COP and Fractal Noise 3D COP: add the Alligator noise type, Jitter and Worley Jitter, and post-processing parameters.\n\n**Filtering and finishing**\n- Sharpen COP: unsharp-mask sharpening.\n- Convolve 3×3 COP: convolves layer pixels.\n- Surface Dither COP: halftone dithering.\n- Pixelate COP: enlarges pixels.\n- Vignette COP: darkens corners.\n- Defocus COP: camera-like defocus.\n- Tone Map COP: converts HDR luminance to display values.\n- Color Correct COP: color corrections.\n- Font COP: adds Smoothing parameters for anti-aliasing rasterized curves.\n\n**Data and VDB conversion**\n- Layer from VDB COP and VDB from Layer COP.\n- Layer to Points COP and Layer to VDB Leaf Points COP.\n- VDB Leaf Points COP, VDB Activate from Points COP, VDB Position Map COP, VDB Reshape COP.\n- VDB Visualize COP, VDB Visualize Slice COP, VDB Visualize Tree COP, VDB Visualize Velocity COP.\n- Layer Attribute Create COP: adds a Type parameter. Layer Attribute Delete COP: removes metadata.\n\n**Workflow and cables**\n- Cables let you braid multiple layers into one input and unbraid them later. New nodes: Cable Filter, Cable Merge, Cable Pack, Cable Rename, Cable Sort, Cable Split, Cable Switch, Cable Unpack.\n- Cache COP: in-memory cache for faster playback.\n- Fetch COP: pulls outputs from another COP into the current network.\n- Two Way Switch If Wired COP: switches between inputs based on wiring.\n- Python Snippet COP, Invoke Geometry COP, SOP Invoke COP, SOP Invoke Graph COP.\n- Filter List: quick access to COP effects without a full network.\n- Texture Mask Paint SOP: faster interoperability with COPs.\n- Copernicus Default Settings window: global resolution, precision, border, pixel scale, and VRAM settings."}]},"uuid":"31669bbc-34fb-4c11-8722-ea4e6bd4ba22","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:58.682Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7cd87a24-f632-4d85-a188-6e1fc8e38ba3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"864c189a-854e-430f-af7a-7356ee95db89","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"8cdb0733-2d97-4752-8516-519aa1b66c5a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FsjfBA29fXZE5XQzxRE8Mv","type":"tool_result","content":"# Copernicus in Houdini 22: Texture and Height Map Features\n\n**Tile Pattern**\n- Tile Pattern COP: new Shape Edge Filter (filter scale for cutout edges) and Anti-Aliasing (smooths jagged shape and outline edges).\n\n**Distort, Slope, and Blur**\n- Distort with Adjacency: new, distorts a layer across texture seams.\n- Slope Direction COP: new Space parameter.\n- Blur COP: Units can use local-space units.\n- Slope blur: not covered on this page.\n\n**Adjacency and Seams**\n- Attribute Sample with Adjacency, Distort with Adjacency, Extrapolate with Adjacency, Geometry to Adjacency, Space Transform with Adjacency.\n- Reaction-Diffusion Block Begin, Ripple Block Begin, and Neural Cellular Automata Core also accept adjacency cables.\n\n**Flood Fill and Segmentation**\n- Points from Blobs COP: identifies islands in a layer to create points. This is the closest match on this page.\n- Flood fill: not covered.\n\n**Stamps and Scattering**\n- New: Configure Stamps COP (creates stamp and sprite attributes on points), Stamp Points COP (updated), Scatter Shapes COP (updated).\n- Stamp Points COP: new Space, Z Falloff, Filter Scale, and Sort Stamps by Depth parameters.\n- Scatter Shapes COP: new Treat Mono as Alpha, Post-Jitter, and Random Per Component parameters.\n- Tile Pattern COP: see above.\n\n**Curves**\n- New: Curve Animate 3D COP (interactive Bézier curve drawing and animation), Rasterize Curves COP (updated).\n- Mask from Curves COP: new Invert parameter.\n- Rasterize Curves COP: new Width Attribute, Optional, and Default Value parameters.\n\n**Grunge Maps (all new)**\n- Grunge Aurora COP\n- Grunge Bark Strips COP\n- Grunge Birch Bark COP\n- Grunge Drips COP\n- Grunge Galvanized Steel COP\n- Grunge Layered Noise COP\n- Grunge Leaking Streaks COP\n- Grunge Moisture COP\n- Grunge Mold Spots COP\n- Grunge Pine Bark COP\n- Grunge Rust COP\n- Grunge Rusty Surface COP\n- Grunge Sheets COP\n- Grunge Wipe Trails COP\n\n**Heightfield and Height-Related Nodes**\n- Terrain-specific HeightField COPs: the page points to the Terrains What's new page for the full list, so they aren't named here.\n- New: Height to Caustics COP, Normal to Height COP, Planar Inflate COP, Refract from Height COP, Ocean Spectrum COP, Ocean Evaluate COP.\n- Updated Space parameters: Height to Ambient Occlusion COP, Height to Shadow COP.\n\n**Neural Nodes**\n- New: ML Computer Vision Inference COP, Neural Cellular Automata Core COP, Neural Cellular Automata Decode COP, Neural Layer to Depth (MoGe-2) COP, Neural Layer to Mask (SAM2) COP.\n- Recipes: ML Train Neural Cellular Automata COP recipe, Neural Cellular Automata recipe, Neural Cellular Automata Block recipe.\n\n**Histogram and Statistics**\n- No dedicated histogram or statistics node is listed.\n- Compute Range parameters on Clamp COP, Mono to RGB COP, Quantize COP, and Remap COP set ranges from the input's minimum and maximum values.\n\n**Block and Loop Features**\n- Block Begin COP: Rename Wires Using Output Labels.\n- Block End COP: Iteration Variable, Total Iterations Variable, First Pass Variable, Rename Wires Using Output Labels.\n- Invoke Block COP: Iteration Variable, Total Iterations Variable.\n- Time Loop COP (new): repeats an input frame range as a loop.\n- Time Blend COP, Time Pack COP, and Time Shift COP (all new).\n- Reaction-Diffusion Block Begin, Ripple Block Begin and End, and the Neural Cellular Automata Block recipe.\n\n**Python**\n- No Python snippet is listed.\n- COP Python Handles gained multi-space support (Buffer, Local, Image, Pixel, Texture), `drawable2D.Dragger2D` support for 3D layer transforms, pivot handling across spaces, and better undo.\n\n**ONNX**\n- ONNX Inference COP: supports models over 2GB via an external data file, adds non-float tensor types and content-dependent output sizes, and adds Device ID, Input and Output Tensor Element Data Type, and RGBA Treatment parameters.\n- ML Computer Vision Inference COP (new): applies an ONNX model to detect and mask objects.\n\n**Substance**\n- Not mentioned on this page.\n\n**Other Texture-Relevant Changes**\n- New: Paint 3D COP (beta), Bake Pre-Process COP, Cell Pattern COP, Cellular Noise COP, Cellular Noise 3D COP, Crystal Noise 3D COP, Knit COP, Weave COP, Turing Patterns COP, UV Shape COP, UV Inverse COP, UDIM Pack COP, Laplacian COP, Corner Detect COP, Convolve Filter COP, Curl COP, Curl Noise COP, Curl Noise 3D COP, Solve Poisson COP.\n- Updated: Bake Geometry Textures COP (version 2.0), Triplanar COP, Triplanar Hex Tile COP, Triplanar UV COP, UV Transform COP (fitting parameters), Worley Noise COP and Worley Noise 3D COP (Round Border), Fractal Noise COP and Fractal Noise 3D COP (Fractal Type, Octave Offset, Sparse Convolution), Bubble Noise COP and Cloud Noise 3D COP (Noise Type, Fold).\n- Curvature COP, Derivative COP, and Slope Direction COP: Space parameters.\n- Dilate Erode COP: Units parameter.\n- Extrapolate Boundaries COP: Diffuse Iterations parameter.\n- Renamed: Layer Attribute Create COP is now Layer Property Create COP; Layer Attribute Delete COP is now Layer Property Delete COP."}]},"uuid":"545f082f-566d-4e30-bfe6-96599088039a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:26:59.998Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7cd87a24-f632-4d85-a188-6e1fc8e38ba3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8cdb0733-2d97-4752-8516-519aa1b66c5a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1",