{"parentUuid":"68622d98-e1f4-4df2-aa33-807f4661ea85","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JxqzaoVUvUrbRxuenLDDxm","type":"tool_result","content":"**Presenter:** Nikola Damjanov, a mobile games TD who helped develop Houdini 22's update of 123 new COP nodes.\n\n**Date:** The page doesn't give a date for the talk. The only date is the 2026 copyright footer.\n\n**Topics covered:**\n- **Grunge maps:** Nine texture maps for effects like rust, moisture, leaks, and organic bark strips.\n- **Weave and Knit generators:** Tools that output custom IDs and UVs for complex layered surfaces.\n- **Mask Combine node:** Bundles multiple baked maps into a single cable to blend and procedurally mask assets such as dragons and creature eggs.\n\n**Not covered in this page:** Height maps, tile patterns, slope blur, flood fill, and Substance comparisons are not mentioned in the content provided.\n\n**Workflow advice:** The page's main practical tip is to use the Mask Combine node to bundle baked maps into one cable, which keeps blending and masking of hero assets manageable while preserving artistic control."}]},"uuid":"afcec521-35e3-413c-a27e-43c0edc5fc03","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:11.107Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3d139432-d129-4cac-9fa6-1528969d990c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"68622d98-e1f4-4df2-aa33-807f4661ea85","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"b2def699-a911-4245-a40f-14ffff1c47cb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E61v9PdRnoH9nkVMuD1yej","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SideFX tutorial Copernicus procedural texturing height map tiles bricks Substance Designer workflow 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/learn/collections/copernicus-3/\"},{\"title\":\"Procedural Sponge Material in MaterialX & Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/how-to-make-a-sponge-material-in-houdini-materialx-copernicus-workflow/\"},{\"title\":\"Heightfield Textures\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/contentlibrary/heightfield-textures/\"},{\"title\":\"2\",\"url\":\"https://vimeo.com/1084749425\"},{\"title\":\"Terrains\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/learn/learning-paths/world-building/terrain/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Create Terrains in Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/how-to-create-terrains-in-copernicus/\"},{\"title\":\"Full PBR Material in Copernicus in Under 10 Minutes!\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/full-pbr-material-in-copernicus-in-under-10-minutes-complete-beginner-workflow/\"},{\"title\":\"H22\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/learn/talks/h22-terrains-in-copernicus/\"},{\"title\":\"What’s new Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/20_5/copernicus.html\"},{\"title\":\"Height to Ambient Occlusion Copernicus node\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttoambientocclusion.html\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Texturing with COPs for Substance Designer artists\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/texturing-with-cops-for-substance-designer-artists/\"},{\"title\":\"copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/learn/collections/copernicus-3/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini Copernicus Tutorial - Broken Stone Tiles - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Lt_ogzxrdU&pp=0gcJCdgAo7VqN5tD\"},{\"title\":\"How To Create Tile-Based Textures\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/how-to-create-tile-based-textures/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini Geo To Cops\",\"url\":\"https://goldenlizard.io/blog/houdini-geo-to-cops/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini Stone Tiles - Copernicus Tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://voxyde.com/houdini-nuke-tutorials/houdini-stone-tiles-copernicus/\"},{\"title\":\"Tile Pattern Copernicus node\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/tilepattern.html\"},{\"title\":\"Geometry based Texturing Resources\",\"url\":\"https://procegen.konstantinmagnus.de/geometry-based-texturing-resources\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini Copernicus - Procedural Texturing - Scene Walkthrough - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjOUdUZ8wMs\"},{\"title\":\"textures — rohan dalvi creates\",\"url\":\"https://www.rohandalvi.net/textures\"}]\n\nHere's what I found. The sources are mostly SideFX's own lessons plus a few community tutorials, and they cover your topics well, with one gap noted below.\n\n**Height maps and masks**\n- SideFX's Copernicus collection includes a lesson on generating heightfield masks in the COPs context in Houdini 21. It notes that the process doesn't just work out of the box.\n- A beginner workflow shows how to generate the Height and Base Color first, then build the other essential maps, with topics including generating roughness, normals, and AO.\n\n**Tiles and bricks**\n- SideFX's Tile Pattern COP node generates rectangular tiles for texture patterns. Its Custom Pattern mode can produce brick-wall layouts through a row offset setting.\n- A SideFX tutorial on the same node covers adding per-tile detail and variation using the per-tile UVs the node generates.\n- A community tutorial on bricks shows how to rasterize geometry into Copernicus and make a pile of bricks tileable for game textures. It uses a tile pattern node to preview how tileable the texture is.\n- A broken-stone tile tutorial covers varying tile position, scale, rotation, and slope, then adding gaps and noise.\n\n**Substance Designer comparison**\n- SideFX's most relevant match for your query is a Houdini 22 beginner lesson, recreating a patterned tile material while comparing the workflow with familiar Substance Designer techniques. It covers layered masks, warps, blends, damage, chipping, edge wear, and surface imperfections.\n- The lesson is aimed at artists coming from Substance Designer.\n- A community tutorial makes the same point about blending, saying the approach of using a Max layer merge to combine geometry color with a noise \"soil\" map is exactly how you would create a material in Substance Designer.\n\n**Gaps and caveats**\n- I didn't find a tutorial that combines all three elements (height-map tiles, bricks, and a Substance Designer workflow) in one lesson. The closest matches are the tile-pattern lesson, the brick tutorial, and the Substance-comparison lesson above.\n- The results mix Houdini versions (20.5, 21, 22). Some tutorials are about 1–2 years old, so node names and menus may have changed. The SideFX docs for Houdini 22 are the most current reference.\n- For a Substance-style workflow, the Houdini 22 tile-material lesson is the best starting point.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"72d091cb-ca30-4fd5-b945-a07c64046180","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:16.520Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"3d139432-d129-4cac-9fa6-1528969d990c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b2def699-a911-4245-a40f-14ffff1c47cb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","