{"parentUuid":"4cc42100-006d-426a-b7c5-a8f978bf3318","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015RtjKzppbvpC66obEti6Wc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Copernicus slope blur equivalent \"distort by slope\" recipe Houdini forum odforce\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/distort.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/slopedir.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.sidefx.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/products/whats-new-in-h205/copernicus/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sdfblend.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/latticedeform.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/heighttoambientocclusion.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/lensdistort.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/blur.html\"}]\n\nI didn't find any odforce forum threads for this query. The results are all SideFX documentation, mostly in Japanese, but they do describe the recipe you're asking about.\n\nThe Distort node's docs include a \"Distort By Slope\" recipe. It sets up a Distort COP and a Slope Direction COP, then feeds the Slope Direction output into the Distort node's dir input. The effect pushes the source image away from high values toward low values of a Mono layer that controls the slope.\n\nThe Slope Direction node is the piece that builds the direction map. It converts a height-style Mono layer into a UV layer that represents the slope direction. Its Angle parameter rotates the computed direction after calculation. Setting it to 90 makes the direction follow the hill downward instead of up the slope. Its Scale parameter adjusts the magnitude globally, since heights often don't match the scale needed for valid values.\n\nI couldn't confirm that this recipe is a true equivalent of a slope blur. The sources describe a displacement along a slope direction, not a blur. For a blur-like result, you may need to combine it with the Blur node, which averages pixel values within a region to produce a blur effect.\n\nFor forum discussion, try searching odforce directly for \"Copernicus slope\" or \"COP distort slope,\" or check the SideFX forums.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c4daa6ae-3e05-4679-83f7-8c3c4aa84794","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:39.656Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"97cee3d4-cf3d-4bd9-8f2c-ba9d4eea58ab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4cc42100-006d-426a-b7c5-a8f978bf3318","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f1f5ce84-0980-4197-a175-553f4a71d935","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CzvCnAims6k6nC8m6Hauhr","type":"tool_result","content":"## Outputs\n- **tiles**: the tiled layer.\n- **id**: an ID layer storing ID values. The page doesn't say how IDs are assigned.\n- **uv**: a UV layer storing UV values.\n\nInputs are `size_ref` (sets output size and metadata), `pointmask` (optional mask amount for points), and `stamp0` (optional scaling amount for stamping).\n\n## Main Parameters\n- **Pattern Size / Clip to Size**: area the tiles must cover; clips tiles whose centroid falls outside.\n- **Pattern Type**: presets (Stack, Header, Stretcher, Flemish, American, Monk, English, Windmill, Cross Hatch, Basketwave, Hopscotch, Herringbone, French) or **Custom Pattern**.\n- **Custom Pattern rows/columns**:\n  - *Mode*: Seamless (uses **Divisions**), Tile Count (**Rows**/**Columns**), or Tile Size (**Tile Width**/**Tile Height**).\n  - *Number of Rows / Row #*: per-row Visible, Offset, Reflect Block, Slide Offset, Height.\n  - *Number of Columns / Column #.#*: per-column Visible, Width, Height, Offset, Rotate.\n  - *Use Expression* switches to a text **Pattern Expression**, with flags `-s` (slide), `-h` (height), `-o` (offset), `-v` (visible), `-r` (rotate), and `-r` (reflect). The page lists `-r` for both, so verify before use.\n- **Offset (Position)**: Row Offset, Column Offset, Row Slide Offset (brick-style staggering, with optional per-row variation), and Uniform/Horizontal/Vertical Jitter.\n- **Gap/grout and bevel**: the page doesn't document these directly. **Inset** (Size section) dilates tile edges, and **Round Corners** on the Rectangle shape rounds corners.\n- **Size**: Uniform Scale, Horizontal Scale, Vertical Scale, and Inset, each with Variation. Orient Tiles keeps scaling aligned to tile edges.\n- **Rotation**: Rotate Pattern (whole pattern, degrees), Rotate Tile (per tile, from its center), Rotate Variation, Checkerboard Rotate (alternates 0° and 90°), and Orient Tiles.\n- **Shape**: Shape Class (Basic, Marker, Compound), Stretch Shape, and a shape-specific list. Drawing options are Draw As (Filled, Distance, Gradient, Outline), Anti-Aliasing, and Shape Edge Filter (0 gives hard edges with aliasing; 1 gives expected aliasing for the resolution).\n\n## Per-Tile Random Values\nEach randomized value has a **Set Varying** option (per tile), a **Variation** amount, and a **Seed**:\n- **Value**: Tile Value (per-tile randomization) and Variation; Background Value is fixed.\n- **Position**: Row Slide Offset variation and Jitter.\n- **Rotate**: Rotate Variation (angles fall between Rotate Tile ± Rotate Variation).\n- **Size**: Uniform Scale, Horizontal/Vertical Scale, and Inset variations.\n- **Split Tiles**: Number of Splits, Jitter Scale, and their variations.\n\n## Index Mapping and Pruning\n- **By Tile Order** sets removal order: Default (from bottom-left), Reverse (from top-right), Random (uses Seed), or Shift (uses Offset).\n- **Threshold** (0–1) sets how many tiles are removed; **Negate Selection** inverts the choice.\n- **Every Nth Tile/Row/Column** and **Checkerboard** provide structured removal.\n- The page notes the first tile may not be bottom-left when offsets or custom patterns are used.\n\n## Split Tiles\nIterations, Area Threshold (skips small tiles), Split Threshold (0–1), and Orient Ratio (0 = horizontal, 1 = vertical, 0.5 = both equally)."}]},"uuid":"f8681c05-e67c-46c7-9b0b-06c5c4337bd7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:44.508Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"97cee3d4-cf3d-4bd9-8f2c-ba9d4eea58ab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1f5ce84-0980-4197-a175-5