{"parentUuid":"7d0dcb75-ce2e-42e0-b947-c0ee316cf5e0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UPVHErjQifbKnK1RNq52dJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"sidefx.com forum Copernicus \"Substance Designer\" slope blur flood fill equivalent COPs thread\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/post/434421/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/post/434421/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/topic/97908/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/97908/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/post/432490/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://sidefx.com/forum/post/432501\"},{\"title\":\"検索 - User list\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/topic/97908/lofi/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://sidefx.com/docs/houdini/copernicus/substance_designer.html\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance - plugin for Houdini\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/post/297328/\"}]\n\nI didn't find a dedicated SideFX forum thread that maps Substance Designer's slope blur and flood fill to Copernicus. The closest results are an official SideFX docs page and a third-party plugin thread.\n\n**Official SideFX docs:** A Houdini 21.0 page for Substance 3D Designer users includes a mapping table, and Flood Fill nodes appear in it alongside Ramp, Histogram, and Remap nodes. The excerpt I retrieved doesn't show the specific flood fill setup, so you'll need to open the page for that. It does offer a workaround for Distance nodes: the Feather COP or Extrapolate Boundaries COP can clean up edge outlines.\n\n**COPstance Copernicus Edition (third-party forum thread):** This plugin's author ported the COP2 nodes to Copernicus. The thread is contradictory on slope blur. An early section says there are no Fluid, Simple Perlin, Slope Blur, Tile, and Tile Generator nodes at this time. A later section says another ported node has been added in the new version of COPstance. The later statement is probably the current state, but I'd verify it in the plugin itself.\n\n**Older COP2 plugin version:** An earlier COPstance release (1.4.0, for Houdini 18) added a Slope Blur node, and the author said Blend and Slope Blur nodes are totally identical to Substance Designer's ones. That was the COP2 version, not Copernicus.\n\nIf you want a native setup, start with the SideFX Substance-to-Copernicus page for flood fill. For slope blur, the COPstance Copernicus thread is the best lead, though I couldn't confirm which version of the Copernicus port includes the node.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"30a4fafc-277d-4e6e-9473-78f865a84538","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:57.586Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f03ce9ad-6520-4f3b-a7ae-8ee41ef68f60","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7d0dcb75-ce2e-42e0-b947-c0ee316cf5e0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"935863e1-9e28-45c9-a33d-28c6c3234144","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VUAfR7t8eTTWw1ejQdrxAF","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **source**: The original layer to distort.\n- **dir**: A per-pixel direction to distort along. When connected, it overrides the Direction Type settings.\n- **scale**: A per-pixel scale that multiplies the **Scale** parameter.\n- **mask**: An optional per-pixel mask amount, scaled by the **Mask** parameter.\n\n**Output**\n- **distort**: The distorted layer.\n\n**Key parameters**\n- **Signature, Border, Filter**: Set the accepted layer type, sampling outside the layer bounds, and the sampling filter. Area filters help when distortion shrinks large regions.\n- **Mask**: Blends the new value with the original. The default is 1.\n- **Direction Type**: `Angle` or `Coordinates`. This applies only when there is no `dir` input.\n- **Direction, Normalize Direction**: X/Y direction in image space (for `Coordinates`), with an option to normalize it.\n- **Angle**: Distortion angle (for `Angle`), where 0 is the positive X direction.\n- **Scale**: Overall strength. Negative values trace backward. With only a `source` UV input, it shifts UVs left and right.\n- **Scale by Timestep**: Scales strength by the timestep.\n- **Streak**: Combines pixel values along the distortion path. Options are `Off`, `Blur` (averages samples), `Min` (keeps the smallest value, useful for eroding), and `Max` (keeps the largest, useful for edge roughness).\n- **Use Streak Weight Ramp / Streak Weight**: Weights samples along the trajectory, with the ramp's left side marking the trajectory start.\n- **Pixels per Step**: Enables a more accurate tracing method for curved or varying trajectories.\n- **Maximum Steps**: Caps the number of steps when Pixels per Step is on.\n\nThe page does not describe a \"displace\" mode. Distortion is either fixed-direction or driven by the `dir` input.\n\n**Distort by Slope recipe**\nThis recipe creates a Distort COP and a Slope Direction COP, wired into the Distort COP's `dir` input. The source image is pushed away from larger values of the Mono height layer, toward lower values.\n\n**Iterative or accumulate option?**\nThe page documents no iteration count or repeated-pass setting, so there is no direct equivalent to Substance slope blur. The closest feature is **Streak**, which combines samples along a single distortion path. `Blur` averages them, while `Min` and `Max` select extreme values. This is a one-pass trace, not repeated slope-based accumulation."}]},"uuid":"fd5be08e-50a2-419a-ba8b-c8013d0a23e1","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:27:57.633Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f03ce9ad-6520-4f3b-a7ae-8ee41ef68f60","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"935863e1-9e28-45c9-a33d-28c6c3234144","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
