{"parentUuid":"046aaebf-7c81-43ca-9adb-9dec121a0917","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HMC7ykGBWhoSJr25BksGeJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Adobe Substance 3D plugin for Houdini sbsar Copernicus COP support 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"experienceleague.adobe.com\",\"url\":\"https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d/ecosystem/3d-applications/houdini\"},{\"title\":\"copernicus implementation inside houdini much like cinema 4d 1186898\",\"url\":\"https://community.adobe.com/feature-requests-51/copernicus-implementation-inside-houdini-much-like-cinema-4d-1186898\"},{\"title\":\"User Guide\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-integrations/3d-applications/houdini.html\"},{\"title\":\"www.sidefx.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/tutorials/sidefx-labs-substance-plugin/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/copernicus/substance_designer.html\"},{\"title\":\"sidefx labs substance plugin\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/tutorials/sidefx-labs-substance-plugin/\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://sidefx.com/docs/houdini/copernicus/substance_designer.html\"},{\"title\":\"downloading and installing the plugin\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-integrations/3d-applications/blender/downloading-and-installing-the-plugin.html\"},{\"title\":\"plugin overview ue5\",\"url\":\"https://helpx.adobe.com/substance-3d-integrations/game-engines/unreal-engine/unreal-engine-5/plugin-overview-ue5.html\"}]\n\nI found no evidence of a Copernicus-native SBSAR loader from Adobe or SideFX, though my search didn't cover Houdini release notes, so a newer build may have one.\n\n**What exists:** Adobe's documentation describes the Substance plugin as a way to load Substance Archive files (SBARs) into Houdini in COPs. Adobe's page also says Substance in Houdini is developed by SideFX Labs. The setup instructions are dated, referring to Houdini 17.5 and Houdini 18.0, so they don't reflect current versions.\n\n**Copernicus demand:** A user request on Adobe's community forum from July 2025 asks for a hardware accelerated implementation of a sbsar loader integrated into Houdini using Copernicus. The same poster says the older integration which is implemented in the older COP network was extremely slow and would often crash. This is a feature request with no reported response in the results.\n\n**Copernicus docs:** SideFX's Houdini 21.0 Copernicus documentation covers Copernicus for Substance 3D Designer™ users. It maps Designer nodes to COP equivalents, such as suggesting Feather or Extrapolate Boundaries COPs in place of the Distance node. This is a guide for rebuilding Designer-style work in Copernicus, not a way to load .sbsar files.\n\n**Bottom line:** The SBSAR integration in Houdini still appears to run through the older COP-based plugin maintained by SideFX Labs. Copernicus support for SBSAR loading looked like an unfulfilled request as of these results. To confirm the current status, check the Houdini 21.x release notes and the SideFX Labs Substance plugin page for 2026 updates.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6e140af9-66ba-4d17-93a8-532bae21a163","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:09.096Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"74438376-996d-477c-8768-1adee6e2a554","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"046aaebf-7c81-43ca-9adb-9dec121a0917","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-des