{"parentUuid":"f74bcc5c-1b58-4f49-b117-c8d616cfbb66","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CFLTnB9p2DxjPAMRiLkVe6","type":"tool_result","content":"**Author:** Quantico, a SideFX forum member (posts since November 2018), who develops the COPstance plugin for Houdini.\n\n**What it is:** A Copernicus (COP) version of the COPstance plugin. It contains the same nodes as the earlier COP2 version, rebuilt entirely from Copernicus nodes. Several nodes are ported from Substance Designer, such as Anisotropic Noise, Plasma, Curve, and the Flood Fill family. The FX-Map node is only partly included (just its Quadrant subnode).\n\n**Notable nodes (per the thread):**\n- **Launch (Sept 2024):** Seamless Noise, Tile Pattern, Arc Pavement, Splatter (Circular), FX-Map (Quadrant only), and others. The thread says Fluid, Simple Perlin, Slope Blur, Tile, and Tile Generator were not included at launch.\n- **v1.1 (Oct 26, 2024):** 3D Extruder, Anisotropic Noise, Plasma, Liquid, Slope Blur, and Splatter, plus Seamless Noise improvements.\n- **v1.2 (Dec 6, 2024):** Curved Shape, Height Blend, Multi Directional Warp, Non Uniform Directional Warp, Vector Warp, Quad Transform, Skew, Trapezoid Transform, Histogram Range/Scan/Scan Non-Uniform/Select/Shift, and Curve.\n\n**Correction to the request:** The thread does not list a Tile Generator. It states that Tile Generator was not planned, since the existing Tile Pattern node is more capable. Histogram Scan is included, but only from v1.2.\n\n**Timeline:**\n- **Sept 11, 2024:** Copernicus Edition released.\n- **Sept 23, 2024:** A texture-creation tutorial was posted to the thread.\n- **Oct 26, 2024:** v1.1 released. Same day, a user reported that Splatter nodes were saved as a non-commercial HDA. Quantico updated the files.\n- **Dec 6, 2024:** v1.2 released, along with a free Flood Fill node library to mark the plugin's fifth anniversary.\n\n**Licensing and price:**\n- The price is not stated in the thread.\n- It is distributed as an OTLLC Digital Asset Library, so there is no trial. Access to the file is provided right after purchase.\n- The older COP2 version remains on the site for evaluation.\n- Owners of the old version receive the Copernicus version free, via emailed download instructions.\n- The Flood Fill library is free, downloadable from the COPstance website.\n- The library is cross-platform, not Windows-only as the COP2 version was, and its internal node structure is viewable and editable."}]},"uuid":"9a33743a-703e-4dd3-abbf-1e1505bae8be","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:11.997Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"74438376-996d-477c-8768-1adee6e2a554","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f74bcc5c-1b58-4f49-b117-c8d616cfbb66","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
