{"parentUuid":"c7451709-4771-49c7-b037-34c0ecb378a8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PLBB4BnRDApkbUiDW9RFiT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SideFX Labs Substance Archive node COP2 Copernicus Houdini 21 22 sbsar labs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード コンポジットノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop2/labs--sbs_archive.html\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Labs Substance Archive node in Copernicus ?\",\"url\":\"https://sidefx.com/forum/post/433909\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Labs Substance Archive node in Copernicus ?\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/98869\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Labs Substance Archive node in Copernicus ?\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/post/449311\"},{\"title\":\"Substance Labs Substance Archive node in Copernicus ?\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/topic/98869\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 22.0 Nodes Compositing nodes\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop2/labs--sbs_archive.html\"},{\"title\":\"検索 - User list\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/topic/98869/lofi\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/topic/97908/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/post/432490/\"},{\"title\":\"COPstance Copernicus Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/forum/post/434421/\"}]\n\nThe Labs Substance Archive node is documented as a Copernicus (COPs) node in Houdini 22. The forum threads I found are older and say it was missing, so the timeline is unclear.\n\n**Current documentation (Houdini 22.0):** The node loads Substance Archive files into COPs. Loading a Substance File is as easy as entering the path to your SBAR file into the File Path Parameter. The docs specify that this plugin works with Substance Archive Files, not Substance Files. You create those archives in Substance Designer by publishing the material. The node also handles inputs and multiple graphs. Despite the COP node only having one input, we do support multiple substance inputs. In the case of multiple graphs inside of a single SBAR file, a new graph parameter will show up. For output, The Substance Archive node will generate a new image plane per Output in Substance.\n\n**Houdini 21:** A Japanese-language copy of the Houdini 21.0 node page exists and describes the same basic workflow of reading an SBSAR path into COPs. I didn't find the English 21.0 page in these results, so I can't confirm from this search exactly which version introduced the node.\n\n**Earlier community reports:** A SideFX forum thread asked why there was no Substance node in Copernicus. A staff member replied that Substance for Copernicus hasn't been tackled yet, but I'll raise it with the Labs team. Users in that thread also complained that the old COP2 version was slow at high resolutions. Since the Houdini 22 docs now include the node, the thread appears to predate its release, but I can't confirm the exact date.\n\n**COPstance:** A separate third-party plugin, COPstance, has a Copernicus edition. Its author says these are the same nodes that were in the old COP2 version of the plugin, but now they are completely written using Copernicus nodes. That is a different tool from the Labs node, and it doesn't load SBSAR files.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"01fc9afa-0a4d-49a8-a7d3-8a8f44c5e9a2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:33.131Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"a3e6c755-7117-432c-9cc4-2fe0f4c7bbe4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":