{"parentUuid":"b1404d3f-847f-4482-ac57-356f04cc91b1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V1iqPGc5VdveuWZB5qNmxB","type":"tool_result","content":"**Network type:** The page doesn't name COP2 legacy or Copernicus. It's listed under \"Compositing nodes\" in Houdini 22.0 and refers to \"the COP node,\" so it's a COP node. The page itself is marked \"To be removed in Houdini 24.0.\"\n\n**What it does:** It loads Substance Archive (SBSAR) files into COPs. Substance Archive files, not Substance Files, are generated from Substance Designer by publishing.\n\n**Parameters:**\n- **File Path:** Path to the SBSAR file.\n- **Reload:** Reloads the current SBSAR file.\n- **Size:** Overrides the output size of the SBSAR.\n- **Substance Parameters:** Populated dynamically from the graph.\n- **Graph:** Appears when the archive contains multiple graphs, to choose which one to use.\n- **Input channel parameters:** Let you map which image plane feeds each Substance input. Inputs are name-matched by default.\n- **Name Image Plane from Usage:** Names output planes by usage type instead of output label.\n\n**Outputs:** The node generates one image plane per Substance output. These are viewed from the image plane dropdown in the Composite View tab.\n\n**Inputs:** Although the node has one COP input, multiple Substance inputs arrive as separate image planes. To feed two File nodes, use a Rename COP. The page also suggests gamma correcting inputs with the Gamma node.\n\n**Known issues:**\n- Animated input images are not supported.\n- Visible If parameter expressions for outputs are not supported.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- The `{channel_name}` syntax doesn't work with Mantra. Rename the target channel to C with a Rename COP and reference that node instead.\n\n**Not covered:** The page says nothing about the Substance Engine, resolution beyond the Size override, or performance."}]},"uuid":"6c126d14-c751-4569-9781-61a72a772f42","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:45.493Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"21addc28-764e-4f8e-bb8e-b20c288ec8f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b1404d3f-847f-4482-ac57-356f04cc91b1","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"bf305e05-9b91-4b0d-9893-346c1490454c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DK2VG5Ns3Tdrv4YSpDRUjo","type":"tool_result","content":"**Thread summary: \"Substance Labs Substance Archive node in Copernicus?\"** (SideFX forums, Houdini for Realtime)\n\n**Posts and dates:**\n- **Nov 21, 2024:** Jaro10 asks whether the missing Copernicus Substance node is intentional and whether the old COP2 Substance node can be brought into COP.\n- **Nov 23, 2024:** Antti1999 answers \"Unfortunately, no.\" He says the old COP2 version was slow above 2K, apparently CPU-only, and praises GPU-accelerated .sbsar loading in Houdini.\n- **May 15, 2025:** Matteh asks whether the situation is unchanged and says he is trying it himself. No reply appears.\n- **May 21, 2025:** Danicka (SideFX staff) says \"Substance for Copernicus hasn't been tackled yet\" and will raise it with the Labs team.\n- **July 6, 2025:** mchaloner says sbsar support in Copernicus would be valuable.\n- **Sept 10, 2025:** mchaloner asks for updates. No reply appears.\n\n**Current status:** Not implemented. The last staff reply was in May 2025, and the thread has no later official update.\n\n**Workarounds:** The thread offers none. It does not mention using COP2 inside Copernicus via fetch or cooking .sbsar files to images. The only practical alternative mentioned is the Houdini .sbsar loading Antti1999 described, with Cinema 4D and Redshift cited as a comparison."}]},"uuid":"0a09a8d5-bed4-481e-9f0a-4cdcede6f042","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:28:45.577Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"21addc28-764e-4f8e-bb8e-b20c288ec8f4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf