{"parentUuid":"1a1285e7-2afa-43ed-a165-65d7663f8be3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0114HBVUqBMksjNfovvhdEFy","type":"tool_result","content":"Copernicus (COP) is described as \"a 2D and 3D GPU image processing framework\" that handles layers (single images) and geometry. The page highlights these Houdini 20.5 additions:\n\n- **GPU and compute:** A Vulkan-based geometry rasterizer, OpenCL nodes with OpenCL and Vulkan interoperability, and traditional and compiled (APEX) cooking.\n- **Compositing replacement:** Copernicus nodes are meant to replace Compositing nodes. The old network is now \"COP Network - Old\" and will be deprecated and removed in a future release.\n- **Preview and ML:** Slap comp for interactive and offline previews, plus an ONNX inference engine and image segmentation.\n- **Texture and pattern tools:** Procedural 2D and 3D noise generators, terrain texture creation, interactive Texture Mask Paint, tileable pattern generators, SDF-based shape generators, and nodes that stamp points.\n- **Visualization:** Live results in the 2D viewport, 3D viewport, and Karma, with a customizable framework for viewport filters.\n- **Material authoring:** Support for material creation workflows (including `op:`), direct import of volumes, heightfields, meshes, and attributes, and access to SOP, DOP, LOP, and OP data. Video input is supported through a SOP-like model.\n- **Learning resources:** Content Library scenes such as Warehouse Lights, Texture Synthesis, and Texture Mask Paint demonstrate texture and material workflows.\n\nThe page does not cover the layer types Mono, RGB, UV, and ID, the nodes fractal noise, feather, segment by connectivity, and slope direction, or blocks and feedback. Those items are not in the provided content."}]},"uuid":"5649de2e-6b7e-4fac-83d6-aefec11fc6e7","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:29:02.195Z","serv