{"parentUuid":"881ed264-5796-4242-9d3a-72b292f537c2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EvzrLu1oCAjceHmvsaRaY7","type":"tool_result","content":"**Filter Frequencies** (Copernicus, since 22.0) boosts or suppresses spatial frequencies in an image.\n\n**Parameters**\n- **Signature:** Sets the layer type the node filters.\n- **Scale:** Multiplies the filtered result. Values above 1 boost the kept band, and values below 1 attenuate it. The default is 1.\n- **Frequency:** Sets the center of the kept band as a normalized radial value from 0 (lowest frequencies) to 1 (finest detail). The default is 0.\n- **Width:** Sets the full width of the kept band around Frequency.\n- **Smooth (radial):** Adds a soft falloff at the band edges instead of a hard cutoff, which reduces ringing.\n- **Anisotropy Angle:** Sets the direction of an angular wedge, from 0 to 360 degrees.\n- **Anisotropy Width:** Sets the wedge's angular extent. The default of 360 keeps all directions.\n- **Anisotropy Smooth:** Softens the wedge's angular edges.\n- **Reflect:** Mirrors the wedge to Angle + 180.\n\nThe page does not list explicit low-pass, high-pass, or band-pass modes, or a ramp control. Band behavior comes from Frequency and Width. Setting Frequency near 0 keeps low frequencies, which is effectively low-pass (my inference). Smooth is the only falloff control.\n\n**Inputs**\n- **source:** The image to filter.\n- **filter:** An optional image used directly as the frequency-domain mask. When connected, it disables the Frequency and Anisotropy controls.\n\n**Outputs**\n- **filtered:** The filtered image.\n\n**FFT:** Yes. The node transforms the source into frequency space with an FFT, multiplies by the mask, and transforms back. The page links to the separate Fast Fourier Transform node.\n\n**Periodic borders/tiling:** The page says nothing about periodic boundaries or tiling behavior."}]},"uuid":"2daf124e-ec3e-43ac-bcb3-90a2e4f58ea0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:29:51.077Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8fd79b94-0a43-49a4-86e7-25bec456ab8e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":829,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":5},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"881ed264-5796-4242-9d3a-72b292f537c2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
