{"parentUuid":"7739a7cd-65d2-4a99-87bc-d7b8bca84955","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WmdAAJo5g4NhGkMXWwFj6U","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ControlMat controlled generative approach material capture Vecchio 2024 TOG height normal from single image diffusion\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ControlMat: A Controlled Generative Approach to Material Capture\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.01700\"},{\"title\":\"controlmat controlled generative approach to material capture\",\"url\":\"https://research.adobe.com/publication/controlmat-controlled-generative-approach-to-material-capture\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.01700v3\"},{\"title\":\"ControlMat: A Controlled Generative Approach to Material Capture\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2309.01700v3\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2309.01700v2\"},{\"title\":\"ControlMat: A Controlled Generative Approach to Material Capture\",\"url\":\"https://cdnjs.deepai.org/publication/controlmat-a-controlled-generative-approach-to-material-capture\"},{\"title\":\"ControlMat: A Controlled Generative Approach to Material Capture\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv-vanity.com/papers/2309.01700\"},{\"title\":\"ControlMat: A Controlled Generative Approach to Material Capture\",\"url\":\"https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2309.01700\"},{\"title\":\"giuseppe vecchio\",\"url\":\"https://research.adobe.com/person/giuseppe-vecchio\"}]\n\nControlMat is a 2023 arXiv preprint that was published in ACM Transactions on Graphics (TOG) in 2024, and it matches what you described: a diffusion model that estimates height and normal maps from a single photo.\n\n- **Authors and venue:** Giuseppe Vecchio and six co-authors from Adobe Research. Adobe lists it as an ACM Transactions on Graphics publication dated September 1, 2024. The arXiv record shows the preprint was submitted on 4 Sep 2023 (v1), last revised 27 Jul 2024 (this version, v3).\n- **Input and method:** The system takes a single photograph with uncontrolled illumination as input and conditions a diffusion model to produce tileable, high-resolution physically-based materials.\n- **Outputs:** The model infers both diffuse (Basecolor) and specular (Roughness, Metallic) properties as well as the material mesostructure (Height, Normal, Opacity). So height and normal are among the maps it produces.\n- **Technical contributions:** The authors analyze the behavior of diffusion models for multi-channel outputs, adapt the sampling process to fuse multi-scale information and introduce rolled diffusion to support tileability and patched diffusion for larger outputs.\n- **Evaluation:** The authors report that their approach outperforms recent inference and latent-space-optimization methods.\n- **Training data:** The models were trained using the Substance 3D Materials database, with renderings paired to ground-truth materials.\n\nSupplemental material is listed at gvecchio.com/controlmat.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"436e4e7e-69f6-4b87-addb-92f17375f010","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:05.028Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"67f613b4-4f56-4ca0-9dc2-938645132ab9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":16,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}