{"parentUuid":"87f77c60-0234-45a2-a24c-b9dd6f9cbbb2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DX5ExFGM4xX9miA1izoDpi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"StableNormal reducing variance monocular normal estimation diffusion SIGGRAPH Asia 2024; Marigold depth estimation CVPR 2024 diffusion\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"StableNormal: Reducing Diffusion Variance for Stable and Sharp Normal\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.16864\"},{\"title\":\"is.mpg.de\",\"url\":\"https://is.mpg.de/ps/de/publications?year=2024\"},{\"title\":\"StableNormal: Reducing Diffusion Variance for Stable and Sharp Normal\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.16864v1\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.16864?context=cs\"},{\"title\":\"StableNormal  by Stable-X\",\"url\":\"https://www.sourcepulse.org/projects/2178836\"},{\"title\":\"catalyzex.com\",\"url\":\"https://catalyzex.com/author/Chongjie%20Ye\"},{\"title\":\"get cal\",\"url\":\"https://asia.siggraph.org/2024/wp-content/plugins/linklings_wp_program/get_cal/?id=sess137\"},{\"title\":\"Perceiving Systems Article 2024\",\"url\":\"https://is.mpg.de/publications/stablenormal2024ye\"},{\"title\":\"api.crossref.org\",\"url\":\"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145%2F3687971\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CVPR 2024 (Oral)\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/prs-eth/marigold?ref=aiartweekly\"},{\"title\":\"Repurposing Diffusion-Based Image Generators for Monocular Depth Estimation\",\"url\":\"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/CVPR2024/html/Ke_Repurposing_Diffusion-Based_Image_Generators_for_Monocular_Depth_Estimation_CVPR_2024_paper.html\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JSP-ywu/Marigold\"},{\"title\":\"Ke Repurposing Diffusion Based Image Generators for Monocular Depth Estimation@CVPR2024@CVF\",\"url\":\"https://papers.cool/venue/Ke_Repurposing_Diffusion-Based_Image_Generators_for_Monocular_Depth_Estimation@CVPR2024@CVF\"},{\"title\":\"thecvf.com\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/virtual/2024/poster/31264\"},{\"title\":\"We gratefully acknowledge support from\",\"url\":\"https://export.arxiv.org/abs/2312.02145\"},{\"title\":\"https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fprs eth%2FMarigold\",\"url\":\"https://imaging-plaza.epfl.ch/software/https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fprs-eth%2FMarigold\"},{\"title\":\"cvpr.thecvf.com\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/virtual/2024/oral/32058\"},{\"title\":\"AI prompts\",\"url\":\"https://trendshift.io/admin/repository/ask-ai/5812\"},{\"title\":\"Repurposing Diffusion-Based Image Generators for Monocular Depth Estimation\",\"url\":\"https://mlanthology.org/cvpr/2024/ke2024cvpr-repurposing\"}]\n\n**StableNormal (SIGGRAPH Asia 2024)**\n\n- **Venue:** The paper appeared as ACM Transactions on Graphics, 43(6), and a project listing notes it was Accepted to SIGGRAPH Asia 2024 (Journal Track).\n- **Core idea:** Standard diffusion inference is stochastic, which clashes with the deterministic nature of normal estimation. The authors mitigate the stochasticity of the diffusion process by reducing inference variance, producing \"Stable-and-Sharp\" estimates without any additional ensembling process. Ensembling is the costly step that earlier methods relied on.\n- **Method:** The pipeline is coarse-to-fine. A one-step estimator (YOSO) produces an initial normal map, and a semantic-guided refinement stage (SG-DRN) then recovers geometric detail.\n- **Availability:** Code and models are on Hugging Face under the Stable-X organization. The project is Licensed under Apache-2.0. It also has a faster \"StableNormal-turbo\" variant for 10x faster inference.\n\n**Marigold (CVPR 2024)**\n\n- **Venue:** The paper is Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (CVPR), 2024, pp. 9492-9502. The official repository labels it as CVPR 2024 (Oral, Best Paper Award Candidate).\n- **Core idea:** Marigold is a method for affine-invariant monocular depth estimation that is derived from Stable Diffusion and retains its rich prior knowledge. The authors wanted to test whether generative diffusion priors could improve generalization in depth estimation, since conventional estimators struggle with unfamiliar scenes.\n- **Training:** The estimator can be fine-tuned in a couple of days on a single GPU using only synthetic training data. The paper reports state-of-the-art performance across a wide range of datasets including over 20% performance gains in specific cases.\n- **Updates:** A faster LCM version was released in March 2024, and training code followed in May 2024.\n\n**How they relate:** Both papers adapt Stable Diffusion to dense geometry prediction. Marigold targets depth, while StableNormal targets surface normals and focuses on making diffusion output deterministic and stable. The StableNormal project's benchmarks compare it against GeoWizard, Marigold Normal, GenPercept, and DSINE, so Marigold serves as a baseline in that line of work.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6b9d8339-bc77-4d79-ad49-3cc1c4fad388","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:06.648Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"67f613b4-4f56-4ca0-9dc2-938645132ab9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":16,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Me