{"parentUuid":"351df1db-4e25-4d92-9a34-8b2aa1c6e466","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVUTj1rXmpiH8A4r4PJba1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SIGGRAPH 2025 OR SIGGRAPH 2026 inverse procedural material node graph optimization paper diffusion prior procedural texture\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MaterialFusion: Enhancing Inverse Rendering with Material Diffusion Priors\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.15273v1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Node Graph Optimization Using Differentiable Proxies\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/362089833_Node_Graph_Optimization_Using_Differentiable_Proxies\"},{\"title\":\"The Visual Computer https://doi.org/10.1007/s00371-025-04096-0 RESEARCH\",\"url\":\"http://www.cad.zju.edu.cn/home/weiweixu/wwxu2025.files/IPMGG.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PhotoScene: Photorealistic Material and Lighting Transfer for Indoor Scenes\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2207.00757\"},{\"title\":\"An Inverse Procedural Modeling Pipeline for SVBRDF Maps\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3502431\"},{\"title\":\"Interpretable procedural material graph generation via diffusion models from reference images\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00371-025-04096-0\"},{\"title\":\"SIGGRAPH Conference Papers '25: Proceedings of the Special Interest Group on Computer Graphics and Interactive Techniques Conference Conference Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.siggraph.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Conference-Papers.html\"},{\"title\":\"Node Graph Optimization Using Differentiable Proxies — Lacuna\",\"url\":\"https://lacuna.tiptreesystems.com/work/node-graph-optimization-using-differentiable-proxies/wrk_1c1b76d1a631b2e22a03a32ad13e15d5\"},{\"title\":\"par.nsf.gov\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10356278\"}]\n\nI didn't find a SIGGRAPH 2025 or 2026 paper that matches all of your criteria (inverse procedural material, node graph optimization, diffusion prior, procedural texture). The closest results are below, and none is confirmed as a 2025 or 2026 SIGGRAPH paper.\n\n**Closest matches**\n\n- **Node graph optimization (SIGGRAPH 2022):** Hu et al.'s \"Node Graph Optimization Using Differentiable Proxies\" is the core prior work in this area. It targets the problem that automatically tuning these graphs to match real-world photographs is challenging because many core \"generator\" nodes are non-differentiable. It is the most direct match for node graph optimization, but it is from 2022.\n- **Procedural material generation (SIGGRAPH 2023):** A 2025 paper in The Visual Computer cites Hu et al.'s \"Generating procedural materials from text or image prompts,\" presented at ACM SIGGRAPH 2023. That paper is not a 2025 or 2026 SIGGRAPH paper.\n- **Diffusion for procedural material graphs (journal, 2025):** The Visual Computer paper, \"Interpretable procedural material graph generation via diffusion models from reference images,\" is relevant. Its two-stage framework uses an adapter-based diffusion model to predict procedural nodes, forming an auxiliary graph, which is then refined using a DiffMat-based node parameter optimization method. This is a journal article, not a SIGGRAPH paper, so it may be what you're thinking of, but it doesn't fit the venue.\n- **Diffusion priors for material appearance (SIGGRAPH 2025 listing):** The SIGGRAPH 2025 conference paper listing includes a texturing method that renders multiple views of the object and uses them, together with an appearance-defining text prompt, to condition a diffusion model. Its generated details are backpropagated from the enhanced images to the material parameters via inverse rendering. This matches the diffusion-prior and inverse-rendering part of your query, but it does not use procedural node graphs.\n- **Related non-SIGGRAPH work:** MaterialFusion uses a diffusion prior with an inverse rendering framework, using score distillation sampling (SDS) to guide the optimization of the albedo and materials. Its venue is not stated in the results.\n\n**Suggested next steps**\n\n- Check the SIGGRAPH 2025 technical papers program and the ACM Digital Library for \"procedural material\" and \"node graph.\"\n- Look for SIGGRAPH 2026 accepted papers, which may not yet be indexed in these results.\n- Search for \"DiffMat\" and \"MATch\" for follow-up work that cites the 2022 and 2023 papers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9f501b38-02b8-4e4e-8a7f-a12f51dc684a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:21.189Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"28ee306a-fb56-44b4-b606-dff9595bfc9d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":18,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"351df1db-4e25-4d92-9a34-8b2aa1c6e466","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
