{"parentUuid":"65f098f8-b30a-4759-8679-6709d1349787","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W61bXSqsgWUR9xiZgfXuyf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"A Bayesian Inference Framework for Procedural Material Parameter Estimation\" Guo Hašan Yan Zhao 2020 summary function MCMC\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Bayesian Inference Framework for Procedural Material Parameter Estimation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.01067\"},{\"title\":\"A Bayesian Inference Framework for Procedural Material Parameter Estimation\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/items/3ee3d980-1dcd-4889-a98f-dd84ce432116/full\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.01067v3\"},{\"title\":\"A Bayesian Inference Framework for Procedural Material Parameter Estimation\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org:443/handle/10.1111/cgf14142\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.01067v3\"},{\"title\":\"graphics.ics.uci.edu\",\"url\":\"https://graphics.ics.uci.edu/publication.html\"},{\"title\":\"api.crossref.org\",\"url\":\"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145%2F3414685.3417781\"},{\"title\":\"3ee3d980 1dcd 4889 a98f dd84ce432116\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/signposting/describedby/3ee3d980-1dcd-4889-a98f-dd84ce432116\"},{\"title\":\"skip to main content\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/biblio/10278366\"},{\"title\":\"skip to main content\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/biblio/10278366-bayesian-inference-framework-procedural-material-parameter-estimation\"}]\n\nI found the paper and its publication details, and the abstract covers the MCMC component you asked about.\n\n**Publication details:** The paper was published in *Computer Graphics Forum* in 2020, volume 39, issue 7, pages 255–266 (DOI 10.1111/cgf.14142). It was presented at Pacific Graphics 2020. The arXiv preprint is 1912.01067. The authors are listed as Yu Guo, Miloš Hašan, Lingqi Yan, and Shuang Zhao; some catalogs spell Hašan as \"Hasan.\"\n\n**Summary:** The paper treats estimating procedural material parameters from photographs as an inverse rendering problem within a Bayesian framework. Rather than producing only a single best fit, the method draws samples from the space of plausible parameters, so a user gets several candidate matches to pick from. The authors apply it to materials such as wall plaster, leather, wood, anisotropic brushed metal, and layered metallic paint, using both synthetic and real target images.\n\n**On the MCMC part:** The framework computes point estimates through optimization and also uses a Markov Chain Monte Carlo method to explore the parameter space. The authors say this approach handles both discrete and continuous model parameters. The search results only include the abstract and front matter, so I can't confirm the specific sampler design or its convergence details. The full PDF on arXiv or the Eurographics DOI page would have those.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"12e7e2ae-a4da-4fe7-8b14-83b32f023e43","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:47.641Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0c524a1a-37f0-4c98-b9fd-64559459d9b7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":18,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToo