{"parentUuid":"d39f71f4-ee55-4f4c-8d50-5b066b97c609","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7QLSCNeBogLSHZ2HR5d6Q","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Lefebvre Poulin 2000 \"Analysis and Synthesis of Structural Textures\" bricks wood parameters; Bourque Dudek 2004 \"Procedural Texture Matching and Transformation\"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"gi2000 12\",\"url\":\"https://graphicsinterface.org/wp-content/uploads/gi2000-12.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"graphicsinterface.org\",\"url\":\"https://graphicsinterface.org/?p=2781\"},{\"title\":\"Generating Physically Stable and Buildable Brick Structures from Text\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.05469\"},{\"title\":\"homepages.loria.fr\",\"url\":\"https://homepages.loria.fr/SHornus/TEXRESIZE/texresize.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"“By-example synthesis of architectural textures” by Lefebvre, Hornus and Lasram – ACM SIGGRAPH HISTORY ARCHIVES\",\"url\":\"https://history.siggraph.org/?p=105499\"},{\"title\":\"sperl 2013 BA\",\"url\":\"https://www.cg.tuwien.ac.at/research/publications/2013/sperl-2013-BA/\"},{\"title\":\"Anisotropic Solid Texture Synthesis Using Orthogonal 2D Views\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/items/cdcde425-3253-4aed-8802-d9001d5e783b\"},{\"title\":\"synapsesocial.com\",\"url\":\"https://synapsesocial.com/papers/W1993614171\"},{\"title\":\"api.crossref.org\",\"url\":\"https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1145%2F2766984\"},{\"title\":\"Anisotropic Solid Texture Synthesis Using Orthogonal 2D Views\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org:443/xmlui/handle/10.2312/8477\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Procedural Texture Matching and Transformation\",\"url\":\"https://diglib.eg.org/handle/10.2312/CGF.v23i3pp461-468\"},{\"title\":\"cim.mcgill.ca\",\"url\":\"https://cim.mcgill.ca/~MRL/pubs/ericb/eg2004.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"escholarship.mcgill.ca\",\"url\":\"https://escholarship.mcgill.ca/downloads/8g84mr63j\"},{\"title\":\"eric bourque\",\"url\":\"https://ixdf.org/literature/author/eric-bourque\"},{\"title\":\"library.cim.mcgill.ca\",\"url\":\"https://library.cim.mcgill.ca/data/websites/Mobile%20Robotics%20Lab/pubs/ericb/vi2001.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"vi2001 bib\",\"url\":\"https://library.cim.mcgill.ca/data/websites/Mobile%20Robotics%20Lab/pubs/ericb/vi2001_bib.txt\"},{\"title\":\"vi2001 bib\",\"url\":\"https://library.cim.mcgill.ca/data/websites/Mobile%20Robotics%20Lab%20(circa%202026)/pubs/ericb/vi2001_bib.txt\"},{\"title\":\"eg2004 abs\",\"url\":\"https://cim.mcgill.ca/~mrl/pubs/ericb/eg2004_abs.html\"},{\"title\":\"spiedigitallibrary.org\",\"url\":\"https://spiedigitallibrary.org/conference-proceedings-of-spie/5444/0000/A-procedural-texture-generation-method-based-on-genetic-programming/10.1117/12.561110.full\"}]\n\nI found both papers and their abstracts. The search did not return full texts, so I can't confirm details of the methods beyond the abstracts.\n\n**Lefebvre & Poulin (2000), \"Analysis and Synthesis of Structural Textures\"**\nThis is a Graphics Interface 2000 paper, pp. 77-86, from Université de Montréal. It presents a system that automatically extracts parameter values for structural textures from photographs, letting the user guide the algorithms. The two procedural texture classes studied are rectangular tilings and wood. The paper's motivation is that non-parametric synthesis methods usually fail on repetitive patterns such as bricks, where the semantics of the features (mortar lines, brick size and shape, regular tiling) is lost. Later work cites it as the approach that proposes to learn the parameters from existing images for specific materials.\n\n**Bourque & Dudek (2004), \"Procedural Texture Matching and Transformation\"**\nThis paper appeared in Computer Graphics Forum, vol. 23, no. 3, pp. 461-468. It addresses creating a smoothly varying sequence of procedural textures that interpolates between arbitrary input texture samples. The method uses a library of procedural shaders and selects the appropriate shaders and their parameters. It samples a shader's parameter domain using a texture similarity function to build a smooth path through the shader's texture range. For transitions between several shaders, it finds jump points that connect them smoothly in texture space.\n\n**How they relate**\nBoth papers fit procedural texture parameters to real-world image samples, which is why they are often grouped together. Lefebvre & Poulin extract parameters from photographs for specific structural classes (tilings such as bricks, and wood). Bourque & Dudek instead search a shader library to match arbitrary samples and interpolate between them. A related 2001 precursor by the same Bourque & Dudek group, \"Image-Driven Procedural Texture Specification,\" is also listed in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9296f7a5-a2b7-4e9e-bad9-6ae626a839ff","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:30:49.350Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0c524a1a-37f0-4c98-b9fd-64559459d9b7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":18,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d39f71f4-ee55-4f4c-8d50-5b066b97c609","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypo