{"parentUuid":"a1a7cba8-a6a8-4280-a9c5-efe26f8dafc0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Py5iVNSxvn1f4CvgW8Wapz","type":"tool_result","content":"**Rasterize Curves COP** rasterizes curves onto a layer and can also rasterize arbitrary attributes. Input curves can be polygonal, Bézier, or NURBS. The node's description is \"Rasterizes curves onto a layer.\"\n\n**Inputs**\n- **curves:** The geometry to rasterize, usually from a SOP Import COP.\n- **camera_ref (optional):** Camera metadata that sets the raster view. Without it, the COPnet's resolution is used, with the camera at the origin looking down the negative Z axis.\n\n**Output**\n- **output1:** The rasterized attributes.\n\n**Width**\n- **Units:** Image Space (default) or Pixels.\n- **Width:** The output line width. If the curves have a width attribute, this value acts as a multiplier.\n- **Width Attribute:** The attribute that drives width, defaulting to \"Width.\"\n\n**Curve shape**\n- **Joints:** Round (default) or Sharp. Max Joint Scale limits how far sharp corners extend, preventing spikes.\n- **Endpoints:** Flat (default) or Round caps.\n- **Resample:** Smooths curves by splitting them into segments of a set length.\n- **Treat Polygons As:** Straight, Subdivision (smooths without passing through original points), or Interpolating (passes through points but can oscillate). Resample by Polygon Edge keeps corners intact.\n\n**Attribute and UV behavior**\n- **Scale V by Width:** Controls the V channel of `intrinsic:uv` output. Options are No Scaling (default), Average, Maximum, or Minimum width along each curve.\n- **Force Tilable V:** Rounds V down to an integer so the result tiles.\n\n**Attribute output**\n- Each attribute entry has an Output Type, a Name that must match an attribute on the curves, and an Optional toggle with a Default Value fallback.\n- Rasterizable attributes must be integer or float with four or fewer components.\n- Special tokens generate layers directly:\n  - `intrinsic:alpha`: pixels hit by the curves.\n  - `intrinsic:depth_ndc`: depth in Vulkan device coordinates.\n  - `intrinsic:depth_eye`: world-space depth.\n\n**Quick Setups**\nButtons add common outputs: Alpha, Position (P), Normal (N), UV, and Depth from Eye. Move to Origin shifts output layers to canonical space.\n\n**Not covered on this page:** falloff or profile controls for the curve cross-section, and antialiasing settings."}]},"uuid":"ad4f07d9-d98f-4eed-ab0f-423e9004441b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:26.564Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0c97b4c9-81b4-4061-bf49-73435d71118c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1a7cba8-a6a8-4280-a9c5-efe26f8dafc0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ed8004e2-78ae-4b2b-b18f-af56bae92224","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GYqwxWB5dAEAhwUuiSqRNY","type":"tool_result","content":"**Inputs**\n- **Image file:** The default source. You set the file path under *Image Input* and can scale it with *Scale to Size*.\n- **COP:** *COP Path* points to a COP, and *COP Frame* and *Planes* choose the frames and channels to use.\n- **Heightfield:** Wiring geometry into the node traces a 2D volume from the input instead. The page says \"If geometry is wired to this, it will instead trace one of the 2d volumes in the input.\" *Layer to Trace* picks the layer by name or number. It must be a 2D volume, such as one from the heightfield tools or Volume Slice.\n\n**Trace controls**\n- *Threshold* sets the minimum brightness that gets traced.\n- *Channel* chooses Mono brightness or the Red, Green, Blue, or Alpha channel.\n- *Translate, Scale, and Rotate* position the traced image. The image is fit to a 1.0 X/Y square.\n\n**Output**\n- The page describes the output as a set of faces around areas above the threshold, not as curves. Its outlines are polygons.\n- *Fit to Curves* maps Bézier curves to the trace, and *Convert to Poly* turns that result into polygons.\n\n**Filters (smoothing and resampling)**\n- *Resample Shapes* with *Step Size* sets the spacing between points.\n- *Smooth Shapes* with *Corner Delta* rounds corners.\n- *Fitting Error* controls curve-fit accuracy, and *Level of Detail* sets polygon point density.\n- *Remove Borders* with *Border Width*, *Hole Faces* (bridges holes), and *Boundary Color* refine the result.\n\n**Copernicus**\n- The page doesn't use the term \"Copernicus.\" It describes a COP input through *COP Path*, so a COP network can serve as the source. The page doesn't say whether that is the same thing as a Copernicus layer.\n\n[WebFetch note: this page's text is 240884 characters long and the answer above covers only characters 0 to 100000; the final 140884 were not read — to read on, call WebFetch again with the same url and offset: 100000.]"}]},"uuid":"d96e46d0-7575-419e-b904-a9f2e6e4402b","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:31:27.935Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0c97b4c9-81b4-4061-bf49-73435d71118c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed8004e2-78ae-4b2b-b18f-af56bae92224","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
