{"parentUuid":"3ad00526-e341-4f1a-adde-c20f457fe0f5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TN2WgVr27k9hf9NgFK1SAw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"odforce Copernicus COPs slope blur flood fill tile height map thread\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Faceting in Displacement Map From Copernicus - General Houdini Questions - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/57151-faceting-in-displacement-map-from-copernicus/\"},{\"title\":\"Zoom / Radial Blur COP - Compositing - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/67448-zoom-radial-blur-cop/\"},{\"title\":\"[Solved] HF Layer to COPs, normalize hight - Compositing - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/45824-solved-hf-layer-to-cops-normalize-hight/\"},{\"title\":\"Topographic map - General Houdini Questions - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/51220-topographic-map/\"},{\"title\":\"konstantin magnus's Content - Page 9 - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/profile/10570-konstantin-magnus/content/page/9/?type=forums_topic_post\"},{\"title\":\"how would i apply a disparity map in cops? - Compositing - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/21136-how-would-i-apply-a-disparity-map-in-cops/\"},{\"title\":\"Workflow for COP Velocity Blur node (velblur)? - Compositing - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/26600-workflow-for-cop-velocity-blur-node-velblur/\"},{\"title\":\"Can Houdini do DOF and Motion Blur in COP? - Compositing - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/12004-can-houdini-do-dof-and-motion-blur-in-cop/\"},{\"title\":\"Composite COP node in HDA crashes Houdini - Pipeline - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/39943-composite-cop-node-in-hda-crashes-houdini/\"},{\"title\":\"Paint Texture Maps in COP's - General Houdini Questions - od|forum\",\"url\":\"https://forums.odforce.net/topic/22228-paint-texture-maps-in-cops/\"}]\n\nI didn't find a thread that matches all of your terms (slope blur, flood fill, tile, height map) in one place. The closest results were about related height-map and blur workflows, mostly in older COP (pre-Copernicus) networks:\n\n- **Heightmap tile in an HDA:** One thread covers reading a heightmap, editing a region of it, and writing it back. The poster says a Composite COP step leaves black bars or crashes Houdini, and the export fails with a bake error. They wanted to edit a specific area because an 8x8k heightfield seems a bit too heavy. This is the closest match to your \"tile height map\" idea.\n- **Height field to COP:** A reply suggests that you can bake a Heightfield to a COP height map of relief and change the pixel resolution. Another thread says a SOP Import of height data can come in as a plain white image unless you create a normalized attribute first. The suggested fix is a fit-range step in VEX that writes the result to a color attribute. There is also a \"remap range\" function right in the SOP import.\n- **Blur:** A user built a Zoom/Radial Blur COP because writing the radial sampling in a wrangle was about 30 lines of boilerplate. The thread is dated 169 days ago. A depth map can feed a Depth of Field COP, and then into a Blur or Defocus COP's mask input. The Velocity Blur COP is described as not working as expected.\n- **Copernicus displacement:** A thread on displacement from high and low poly meshes in Copernicus reports faceting on the rendered result. The poster notes that Copernicus was in beta at the time and had many crashes.\n- **Flood fill:** None of the results mention flood fill.\n\nI ran one search, so these are not a complete survey. If you want, I can search for a narrower phrase, such as \"Copernicus flood fill\" or \"COP slope height map\", to look for a thread that covers the exact combination.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2181c90e-3a04-408d-bd19-6202db27429c","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:16.907Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"104546c8-3deb-4d0f-b512-cf4e625261c2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":24,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ad00526-e341-4f1a-adde-c20f457fe0f5","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"0d7fac1a-d97a-4f57-be64-4c73abfe6701","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HDW8Q5pkWyXH367ToNCMwE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"sidefx forum Copernicus flood fill random gradient per tile height bevel \"segment by connectivity\" uv map by id\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 Copernicus\",\"url\":\"https://sidefx.com/docs/houdini/copernicus/substance_designer.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Ultimate Copernicus Guide | Every COP Node Explained\",\"url\":\"https://vimeo.com/1033915968\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 21.0 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/segmentbyconnectivity.html\"},{\"title\":\"Copernicus: White mono islands to id?\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/97374/?page=1\"},{\"title\":\"Copernicus: White mono islands to id?\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/topic/97374\"},{\"title\":\"Copernicus: White mono islands to id?\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/forum/post/427967\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/rgbatouv.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/idtosdf.html\"},{\"title\":\"Houdini 20.5 ノード Copernicusノード\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidefx.com/ja/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/uvxform.html\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a single forum thread covering the whole workflow (flood fill, random gradient per tile, bevel, segment by connectivity, and UV map by ID together). It did surface relevant pieces.\n\n**Node mapping for Substance Designer users:** SideFX's Copernicus guide for Substance 3D Designer users pairs Designer's Flood Fill, Gradient, Ramp, and Segment by Connectivity / UV Map by ID nodes with their Copernicus equivalents. Gradient nodes, Ramp nodes, Histogram nodes, Remap nodes, Flood Fill nodes, Segment by Connectivity and UV Map by ID nodes are all listed there. It also covers edge cleanup: you can use the Feather COP or Extrapolate Boundaries COP to clean up the edges' outline instead of Designer's Distance node.\n\n**Segment by Connectivity:** This is the node that turns a flat mask into separate regions. It breaks the incoming layer into connected components according to a rule. Its Connectivity setting controls what counts as connected, with options such as pixels connected if they are in the same \"band\" of values, where each band is of size Threshold. Its id output gives a unique integer greater than or equal to zero for each connected region.\n\n**Forum thread:** The closest SideFX forum match is \"Copernicus: White mono islands to id?\" It uses the Segment by Connectivity node to convert white mono islands into ID values, which is the same step a flood fill workflow needs before per-island work. The thread text mostly repeats the node documentation, so I couldn't confirm the user-level workflow details from it.\n\n**UV Map by ID:** The UV Transform COP documentation (Japanese page) says each pixel can get its own randomized transform, which lets you transform the island groups created by UV Map by ID individually. That is the mechanism for per-tile random variation after you've made IDs.\n\n**Not found:** I found no SideFX forum or documentation result covering a random gradient per tile height setup or a bevel step in Copernicus. The Copernicus video guide lists Tile Pattern, Segment by Connectivity, Fill, Smooth Fill, and Feather nodes, but doesn't describe those specific setups. You can also use the Feather COP to expand and shrink shapes. That may be a workable stand-in for a bevel-like edge, but it's an untested suggestion from me, not a documented method.\n\nFor a full answer, I'd search the SideFX forum directly for \"random per tile\" or \"tile height\" in Copernicus threads, or post your network as a question.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"62524f2b-9bcb-4752-986b-cafc7fb24a34","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:33:20.032Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"104546c8-3deb-4d0f-b512-cf4e625261c2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":24,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"matthieuhuguet/Memory","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d7fac1a-d97a-4f57-be64-4c73abfe6701","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
