{"parentUuid":"950f1370-8260-4943-97b1-fdab932eabef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YMATCvg73NNbwcqpZ2qRdx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"DiffMat: Latent diffusion models for image-guided material generation\" Visual Informatics 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Visual Informatics (Mar 2024)\",\"url\":\"https://doaj.org/article/8991ecdba19b4489a679fdc14388e4d3\"},{\"title\":\"DiffMat: Latent Diffusion Models for Image-Guided Material Generation\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/en/?p=3452\"},{\"title\":\"fj.ics.keio.ac.jp\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/en/?p=18474\"},{\"title\":\"2024 international journal\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/en/archives/tag/vis-inf\"},{\"title\":\"2024 国際 学術誌\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/archives/tag/vis-inf\"},{\"title\":\"2024 international journal\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/en/archives/date/2024/03\"},{\"title\":\"fj.ics.keio.ac.jp\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/archives/date/2024/03\"},{\"title\":\"2024 国際 発表\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/ja/archives/category/2024\"},{\"title\":\"fj.ics.keio.ac.jp\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/publication/archives/tag/gp/page/2\"},{\"title\":\"fj.ics.keio.ac.jp\",\"url\":\"https://fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/en/?p=17509\"}]\n\nThe paper is in Visual Informatics, Vol. 8, No. 1, pp. 6–14, published in March 2024. The authors are Liang Yuan, Dingkun Yan, Suguru Saito, and Issei Fujishiro. A Keio University lab page lists it as March 30, 2024 (journal pre-proof online on January 4, 2024).\n\n**Problem addressed:** Existing material capture and conditional generation methods depend on flash-lit photos, so their output degrades when the lighting in a reference image differs from the training data.\n\n**Approach:** The model pairs a CLIP image encoder with a multi-layer, cross-attention denoising backbone. It generates latent materials from images taken under varied illumination. A pre-trained StyleGAN-based material generator then turns those latents into high-resolution SVBRDF textures, which fit standard physically based rendering pipelines and need less compute and data than training from scratch.\n\n**Reported results:** The authors say the method surpasses existing generative methods in terms of material quality and variety, and shows adaptability to a broader spectrum of lighting conditions in reference images.\n\n**Where to read it:** The abstract is on DOAJ (doaj.org/article/8991ecdba19b4489a679fdc14388e4d3). The Keio lab summary page (fj.ics.keio.ac.jp/en/?p=18474) gives a shorter overview. I did not retrieve the full text, so details beyond the abstract are unverified.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"735b6407-2855-452a-8e15-62ecc73e8807","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:37:33.502Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"74c9a033-2612-43d0-8b90-b4dbf51b2ff9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"950f1370-8260-4943-97b1-fdab932eabef","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
