ine takes spatially varying BRDF material maps and converts them into procedural models. It breaks the input into a tree of sub-materials, and each decomposed sub-material is proceduralized by a novel multi-layer noise model. A differentiable rendering optimization then recombines these procedures so they match the original pixel maps. The result is a fully procedural material that can be edited, and the authors say it avoids the artist designed material graphs required in previous work.\n\n**Where to read it:**\n- Preprint PDF from Yale: graphics.cs.yale.edu/sites/default/files/ipmm_preprint.pdf\n- arXiv: arXiv:2109.06395 (first submitted September 2021)\n- Adobe Research publication page, which lists the publication date as December 15, 2021\n\nThe search results did not include the final ACM-published version, so check the ACM Digital Library for the definitive citation and page numbers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"14507ae4-db08-4d41-8a9d-ee57deac3187","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:37:34.533Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"74c9a033-2612-43d0-8b90-b4dbf51b2ff9","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad8bd2ca-df42-4faf-8535-813e97394273","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
