ing colors. That matching constraint is what lets a small tile set join into a seamless plane.\n\n**Non-periodic tiling:** The authors present a new stochastic algorithm to nonperiodically tile the plane with a small set of Wang Tiles at runtime. Filled tiles can then produce large textures efficiently at runtime, which is the main advantage the paper claims.\n\n**Other contributions:** The paper also covers filling tiles with 2D texture, 2D Poisson distributions, or 3D geometry. It additionally extends the definition to include a coding of the tile corners to allow discrete objects to overlap more than one edge.\n\n**Caveats:** A Java texture-synthesis plugin's documentation notes that some required details of the algorithms weren't explained thoroughly in the paper so these had to be guessed, invented or otherwise generated. A patent document also lists a known limitation of Wang-tile methods: diamond shaped artefacts, which accompany the generation of Wang Tiles are often apparent.\n\nI did not retrieve the full PDF, so the details of the stochastic selection rule itself are not covered here. The authors' PDF is linked from the University of Konstanz project page (graphics.uni-konstanz.de).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cb099f1f-2791-44a9-9561-ad872ca25eaf","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:48.859Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7885e881-de74-49af-a6ee-c7f96a2a3dad","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"43a2ce3a-ada0-4d72-a6c5-020a9f5cfb91","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e9