{"parentUuid":"8f23c8ef-6ee0-4e02-8492-e9cf6924762a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f51e2112-0260-44ed-9b89-c69d1eac8b4d","agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6EL3FnpWoo5iuRznwUzPF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Efros Leung 1999 texture synthesis non-parametric sampling window size Markov random field; Efros Freeman 2001 image quilting minimum error boundary cut\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"www.cs.princeton.edu\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/fall14/cos526/papers/efros99.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.cs.ubc.ca\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.ubc.ca/~lowe/425/efrosLeung99.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Texture Synthesis by Non-parametric Sampling\",\"url\":\"https://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~efros/research/EfrosLeung.html\"},{\"title\":\"PAPER DIGEST\",\"url\":\"https://www.paperdigest.org/certificate/9316f52a7604a6d9\"},{\"title\":\"陳煥宗 電腦視覺特效▕ 第三周課程資料 TextureSynthesis\",\"url\":\"https://ocw.nthu.edu.tw/ocw/upload/125/1459/陳煥宗 電腦視覺特效▕ 第三周課程資料_TextureSynthesis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"docs.google.com\",\"url\":\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1FCfqNQd0_LNZ1PEtdi_mWsGbOfTVFKBz/htmlpresent\"},{\"title\":\"07 texture\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.princeton.edu/courses/archive/fall14/cos526/lectures/07-texture.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.cs.washington.edu\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.washington.edu/education/courses/576/03sp/lectures/texture.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"courses.cs.washington.edu\",\"url\":\"https://courses.cs.washington.edu/courses/cse576/03sp/lectures/texture.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Texture Synthesis by Non-Parametric Sampling\",\"url\":\"https://mlanthology.org/iccv/1999/efros1999iccv-texture\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"image quilting\",\"url\":\"https://cs.brown.edu/courses/cs129/asgn/proj4_texture_2020/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"陳煥宗 電腦視覺特效▕ 第三周課程資料 TextureTransfer\",\"url\":\"https://ocw.nthu.edu.tw/ocw/upload/125/1459/陳煥宗 電腦視覺特效▕ 第三周課程資料_TextureTransfer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"IAT455 TextureSynthesis ProjectReport\",\"url\":\"https://olc.sfu.ca/sites/default/files/2022-03/IAT455_TextureSynthesis_ProjectReport.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"image quilting\",\"url\":\"https://cs.brown.edu/courses/cs129/2020_Fall/asgn/proj4_texture_2020/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"陳煥宗 電腦視覺特效▕ 第03周課程資料 TextureTransfer\",\"url\":\"https://ocw.nthu.edu.tw/ocw_v3/upload/125/news/陳煥宗 電腦視覺特效▕ 第03周課程資料_TextureTransfer.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cs.brown.edu\",\"url\":\"https://cs.brown.edu/courses/cs129/results/proj4/kloh\"},{\"title\":\"cs.brown.edu\",\"url\":\"https://cs.brown.edu/courses/cs129/results/proj4/njooma\"},{\"title\":\"article lr\",\"url\":\"https://ipol.im/pub/art/2017/171/article_lr.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"gigl.scs.carleton.ca\",\"url\":\"https://gigl.scs.carleton.ca/papers/iiq.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the core ideas of both papers, though neither result set gave the window-size or block-size details you asked about.\n\n**Efros & Leung (ICCV 1999), \"Texture Synthesis by Non-parametric Sampling\"**\n\n- The method grows an image from a small seed, one pixel at a time. The texture synthesis process grows a new image outward from an initial seed, one pixel at a time.\n- It uses a Markov random field assumption. For each pixel, the algorithm estimates the conditional distribution from its already-synthesized neighbors by searching the sample image for similar neighborhoods. A Markov random field model is assumed, and the conditional distribution of a pixel given all its neighbors synthesized so far is estimated by querying the sample image and finding all similar neighborhoods.\n- Sampling from that distribution means picking a match at random. One lecture slide set puts it this way: To sample from this pdf, just pick one match at random.\n- The window size is the neighborhood that gets matched. The lecture materials include a \"Varying Window Size\" slide showing Increasing window size, but the search results did not give the paper's exact window-size guidance or how it is chosen. Check the paper's experiments section for that.\n- Matching uses sum of squared differences: Sum of squared differences (SSD).\n- The degree of randomness is set by one parameter. The degree of randomness is controlled by a single perceptually intuitive parameter.\n\n**Efros & Freeman (SIGGRAPH 2001), \"Image Quilting for Texture Synthesis and Transfer\"**\n\n- The paper works with blocks instead of single pixels. The motivation is that neighbor pixels are highly correlated, so the unit of synthesis becomes a block. The lecture notes add that this is Much faster: synthesize all pixels in a block at once.\n- Blocks are placed in overlapping positions, and each new block must match the overlap region of its neighbors. Source notes describe the process as a patch Pin of I0 that matches Pold on the overlap region is randomly selected. An optimal boundary cut between Pold and Pin is then computed within the overlap region.\n- The minimum error boundary cut is found with dynamic programming. One course slide states to use dynamic programming to compute minimal error boundary cut.\n- The seam then blends the two patches. This optimal boundary cut is used to construct the new patch Pnew by blending Pold and Pin along the cut.\n- The authors describe the approach as taking the source texture's blocks as correct samples and only needing to connect them. In one course summary, the idea is that Texture blocks are by definition correct samples of texture so problem only connecting them together.\n- The method has known failure modes. One analysis reports that the shortcomings of the Efros-Leung algorithm, that is, garbage growing and verbatim copy, are also present in the Efros-Freeman results, but only at a larger scale.\n\n**Gaps:** The results did not give the block-size or overlap-width values Efros & Freeman used, or the exact window-size settings from Efros & Leung. For those, go to the original papers. The Efros & Leung PDF is hosted at Berkeley's Efros research page.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"107ae08a-ad34-4552-b9b5-9cc51deaf51a","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:39:50.032Z","serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7885e881-de74-49af-a6ee-c7f96a2a3dad","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":null,"error":"pending"},"live_cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8f23c8ef-6ee0-4e02-8492-e9cf6924762a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reasonType":"rule"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
