nge, otherwise amplitude errors disappear. (11 October 2026)\n- Step 2, structure masks: threshold the reference at absolute levels chosen on its histogram to obtain the deterministic classes (tile face, bevel ring, grout, raised lines, and the chips and cracks we decide to place exactly); apply the same thresholds to the output. (11 October 2026)\n- Step 3, stochastic residual: estimate it on both images with the same operator, for example the image minus a Gaussian blur of sigma 2 pixels, inside each class eroded by 4 pixels so that edges do not leak into it; σ of the reference residual gives the RMSE floor of 3.1. (11 October 2026)\n- Step 4, self baseline: compute every stochastic metric between two disjoint halves of the reference (left against right, top against bottom, aligned on the tile period); the value B is the reference's own variability, and an output is statistically identical when d(output, reference) stays within a small multiple of B. (11 October 2026)\n- Step 5, gates: evaluate the gates of the table below; a layer is finished when its gate passes, and the work is finished when every gate passes or when the full image RMSE is within 10 percent of the floor. (11 October 2026)\n- Step 6, single score for ranking candidates: score = mean over gates of max(0, m_g / τ_g − 1), with m_g the measured value and τ_g its threshold, after turning \"higher is better\" metrics into 1 − value; zero means all gates pass, and lower is better. (11 October 2026)\n- Step 7, acceptance of a new layer: keep it only if it improves the metric of the gate it targets by at least 5 percent relative, or makes that gate pass, while no other gate worsens by more than 2 percent relative; otherwise revert it and try the next candidate. (11 October 2026)\n- Thresholds below assume a 2048 by 2048 map; pixel tolerances scale with resolution, percentages do not. (11 October 2026)\n\n<table><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Metric</th><th>Computed on</th><th>Threshold (PROPOSED)</th><th>Kind of identity</th><th>Date (11 October 2026)</th></tr>\n<tr><td>A layout</td><td>MAE of 64 by 64 area averaged thumbnails</td><td>whole image</td><td>at most 1.0 percent of r (2.5 percent if low frequency mottling is accepted as stochastic)</td><td>deterministic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>B class geometry</td><td>IoU at absolute thresholds</td><td>each deterministic class</td><td>tile face 0.97, grout 0.90, raised lines 0.85, traced cracks and chips 0.75</td><td>deterministic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>C thin structure</td><td>boundary F1 at 2 pixels</td><td>grout and line masks</td><td>at least 0.90</td><td>deterministic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>D cross sections</td><td>correlation and MAE of averaged profiles</td><td>grout edge with bevel, motif line, row and column means</td><td>correlation at least 0.99 for averaged edge profiles and 0.98 for row and column means, MAE at most 1.0 percent of r</td><td>deterministic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>E per tile values</td><td>MAE of per tile mean height and tilt</td><td>tile IDs</td><td>at most 0.5 percent of r</td><td>deterministic if index mapped, else stochastic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>F amplitude</td><td>W1 of residual histogram, ratio of residual standard deviations</td><td>each class</td><td>W1 at most 0.5 percent of r, ratio between 0.9 and 1.1</td><td>stochastic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>G spectrum</td><td>log10 ratio of RAPS per octave, angular profile L1</td><td>residual inside tile faces</td><td>within plus or minus 0.1 per octave, angular L1 at most 0.10</td><td>stochastic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>H texture</td><td>DISTS or sliced Wasserstein ratio to self baseline</td><td>residual, multi scale</td><td>at most 1.5 times B</td><td>stochastic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>I sparse features</td><td>component count, KS on log areas, skeleton length</td><td>chip, pinhole and crack masks</td><td>count within 10 percent (exact if traced), KS at most 0.15, length within 10 percent</td><td>stochastic or deterministic</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>J floor check</td><td>full image RMSE against the floor</td><td>whole image</td><td>at most 1.1 times the square root of (RMSE_D² + 2σ²)</td><td>both</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr></table>\n\n- Caveat on AI generated references: their grids are often slightly irregular (wavy grout, unequal tiles), which caps gate B and C for a perfect lattice; the remedy is a method that represents the irregularity (per tile index mapping, traced grout, M07 and M08), never a lowered threshold (PROPOSED). (11 October 2026)\n- Caveat on alignment: a global sub pixel shift between output and reference can be removed with `alignpixels` or by phase correlation before the deterministic gates, but local warping must not be applied, since it would hide geometry errors (PROPOSED). (11 October 2026)\nEOF\npython3 -I /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray--claude-Memory1/3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953/scratchpad/check_part.py /Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-height/dataset/parts/08_state_of_the_art_methods.md; echo \"exit=$?\"","description":"Append section 3 metrics and validate format"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e9f68f85-6523-45dc-8322-9336cb1d75ad","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfvdD4rmVuBBYKhfpkhgc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionSkill":"zenray-houdini","type":"assistant","uuid":"6e9313b6-ebfe-4fb1-b26d-c3df6a158318","timestamp":"2026-10-11T14:43:43.541Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/.claude/Memory1","sessionId":"3a9c2407-7dcc-4acd-baf2-90a94300e953","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
