{"parentUuid":"302b89a9-b30e-4ce7-8e68-a71b05634fa5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"ae649ce7dcad97197","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvdMw9vRUNBo6K73rGDg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V9GBav4P6Ni28GT1mCYLtj","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-height/dataset/parts/08_state_of_the_art_methods.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 4. Official SideFX Copernicus resources and Adobe interoperability (11 October 2026)\n\n### 4.1 Copernicus timeline and the nodes that matter for heights (11 October 2026)\n\n- Houdini 20.5 (July 2024): Copernicus arrives, in beta, as a 2D and 3D GPU image processing framework with a Vulkan geometry rasterizer, OpenCL nodes, compiled cooking, ONNX inference and segmentation, procedural 2D and 3D noises, tileable pattern generators, SDF shape generators, point stamping and Texture Mask Paint; it replaces the old compositing network, renamed \"COP Network Old\" and scheduled for removal; the notes list Content Library scenes named Warehouse Lights, Texture Synthesis and Texture Mask Paint (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/20_5/copernicus.html, read; beta status from the 20.5 product page summary). (11 October 2026)\n- Houdini 21 (August 2025): 2D tiling, Hyperbolic Tile, Triplanar Hex Tile, Scatter Shapes, Scatter on Curves, Copy and Transform, Curve 3D, Layer from Curves, Mask from Curves, Rasterize Curves, Bend, Lattice Deform, Fill Connected, Collapse IDs on Segment by Connectivity, Reaction Diffusion and Flow blocks, Block End with Simulate and Live Simulation for feedback loops, Convert Depth, HeightField Visualize, Height to Shadow, height layers shown as heightfields and hillshades, Curvature, new Derivative modes, Edge Detect updates, Phasor, Bubble, Crystal and Cloud noises, Chladni patterns, Alligator noise and Worley jitter in Fractal Noise, Sharpen, Convolve 3x3, Python Snippet, Invoke Geometry, SOP Invoke, cables, Cache, Fetch, Bake Geometry Textures, Ray Trace and UDIM support (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/21/copernicus.html, read; release month from https://digitalproduction.com/2025/08/26/houdini-21-finally-lands-the-buzz-is-over-time-to-actually-use-it/). (11 October 2026)\n- Houdini 22 (announced June 2026): height field tools migrate from SOPs into COPs; new Filter Frequencies (band center, width, smooth falloff, anisotropy wedge, optional frequency domain filter image), Laplacian, Corner Detect, Convolve Filter by FFT, Solve Poisson, Normal to Height, Planar Inflate, Points from Blobs, Cell Pattern, Cellular Noise, Turing Patterns, UV Shape, UV Inverse, Weave, Knit, fourteen Grunge generators, Mask Combine, Configure Stamps; updates to Stamp Points (Space, Z Falloff, Filter Scale, sort by depth), Scatter Shapes (Treat Mono as Alpha, Post Jitter, Random per Component), Tile Pattern (Shape Edge Filter, Anti Aliasing), Fractal Noise (Fractal Type, Octave Offset, Sparse Convolution), Worley (Round Border), Extrapolate Boundaries (Diffuse Iterations), Dilate Erode (Units), Block End and Invoke Block (iteration variables); Time Loop, Time Shift, Time Blend, Time Pack; neural COPs (MoGe 2 depth, SAM2 mask, ML Computer Vision Inference, Neural Cellular Automata), ONNX improvements, Paint 3D (beta) and Bake Pre Process (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/news/22/copernicus.html, read; launch coverage https://www.cgchannel.com/2026/06/sneak-peek-houdini-22/ and https://digitalproduction.com/2026/06/23/here-comes-houdini-22/, titles and summaries only). (11 October 2026)\n- Counting: the Houdini 22 talk \"What's new in Copernicus\" by Nikola Damjanov speaks of 123 new COP nodes and nine grunge maps, whereas the documentation lists fourteen Grunge COPs; the local Houdini 22.0.368 list holds 371 internal names (versioned duplicates included) and fourteen `grunge_` entries, so the documentation count prevails (https://www.sidefx.com/learn/talks/whats-new-in-copernicus/, read). (11 October 2026)\n\n### 4.2 The SideFX page \"Copernicus for Substance 3D Designer users\" (11 October 2026)\n\n- Source: local copy /Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-height/dataset/sidefx_substance_designer_equivalence.txt, online at https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/copernicus/substance_designer.html (read in full). (11 October 2026)\n- Concepts: a Substance package corresponds to a .hip file with subnetworks, a project of SBS files to an HDA, function graphs to VOPs and VEX, grayscale to Mono, frames to network boxes; values Substance calls Attributes appear in the node info window, and values it calls Base parameters appear on the COP Network node only. (11 October 2026)\n\n<table><tr><th>Substance 3D Designer node</th><th>Copernicus equivalent</th><th>Note</th><th>Date (11 October 2026)</th></tr>\n<tr><td>Alpha Merge</td><td><code>blend</code></td><td>Mode Add, alpha wired into bg or fg</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Ambient Occlusion (HBAO)</td><td><code>heighttoambientocclusion</code></td><td>sphere occlusion per pixel</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Auto Levels</td><td><code>equalize</code></td><td>stretches or shifts the range</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Bevel</td><td><code>feather</code></td><td>see the distance use case</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Directional Blur</td><td><code>streakblur</code></td><td>motion blur like streaks</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Distance</td><td><code>feather</code>, <code>extrapolateboundaries</code></td><td>cleaner edges than flood fill of ragged outlines</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Flood Fill family</td><td><code>segmentbyconnectivity</code>, <code>uvmapbyid</code>; <code>randommono</code>, <code>randomrgb</code></td><td>random grayscale or color per island</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Gradient</td><td><code>ramp</code></td><td>linear and radial ramps</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Histogram nodes (Scan, Range, Select)</td><td><code>remap</code></td><td>Operation Threshold for Histogram Scan</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Levels</td><td><code>remap</code></td><td>Compute Range from input added in 22</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Make It Tile</td><td><code>tilepattern</code>, <code>feather</code></td><td>edge cleanup as for Distance</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Min Max</td><td><code>statistics</code></td><td>average, minimum, maximum</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Perlin Noise</td><td><code>fractalnoise</code></td><td>several noise types</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>RGBA Split</td><td><code>channelsplit</code></td><td>Mono outputs</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Shape</td><td><code>sdfshape</code> into <code>sdftomono</code></td><td>SDF first, then a profile</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Slope Blur</td><td>Distort by Slope recipe: <code>slopedir</code> into the dir input of <code>distort</code></td><td>single pass, not iterative (see below)</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Splatter</td><td><code>shapescatter</code>, <code>curvescatter</code></td><td>stamps over the image or along curves</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tile Generator</td><td><code>tilepattern</code></td><td>rectangular tiles with id and uv outputs</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Tile Sampler</td><td><code>shapescatter</code></td><td>stamping inputs</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Uniform Color</td><td><code>constant</code></td><td>constant layer</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Warp</td><td><code>distort</code></td><td>direction from angle, coordinates or a dir input</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Dot (portal), Output</td><td><code>null</code>, <code>fetch</code>, <code>rop_image</code></td><td>routing and writing to disk</td><td>11 October 2026</td></tr></table>\n\n- Use case, distance like cleanup with Feather: Tile Pattern tiles into the Feather source; Feather Direction set to Circle for smoother results; Feather from High to Low expands outer edges into the background; Distance for Unit Change sets the falloff; followed by a Remap with Operation Threshold and Threshold When Greater, the same chain grows or shrinks shapes. (11 October 2026)\n- Use case, Extrapolate Boundaries: the design goes into source, the base shape into fillarea (blurred first to avoid grainy small segments), the cracks into mask so that blending stays inside them; Exterior set to Unchanged; Threshold and Edge Padding tuned by eye; when fillarea is the inverse of source, Edge Padding grows each dot until it meets the next, which yields cell patterns. (11 October 2026)\n- Slope blur in detail: the Distort COP (documentation read) offers Streak modes Off, Blur, Min and Max that combine samples along one traced path, Pixels per Step for curved trajectories and Maximum Steps, but no iteration count; the Distort by Slope recipe pushes values away from high toward low areas of the Mono height that feeds Slope Direction; an iterated Substance style slope blur therefore needs several chained Distort nodes or a feedback block (Block End with Simulate, Houdini 21), equivalence UNVERIFIED (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/distort.html). (11 October 2026)\n- Slope Direction converts a Mono height into a UV direction layer, with an Angle to rotate the direction, a Scale for magnitude, and a Space parameter added in Houdini 22 (Japanese documentation summary and the H22 news page). (11 October 2026)\n\n### 4.3 Tile Pattern COP, the generator closest to a tile height (11 October 2026)\n\n- Outputs `tiles`, `id`, `uv`; inputs `size_ref`, `pointmask`, `stamp0` (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/tilepattern.html, read). (11 October 2026)\n- Layout: presets Stack, Header, Stretcher, Flemish, American, Monk, English, Windmill, Cross Hatch, Basketweave, Hopscotch, Herringbone and French, or Custom Pattern in Seamless, Tile Count or Tile Size mode with per row and per column visibility, offset, slide, height, width and rotation, or a text Pattern Expression. (11 October 2026)\n- Variation: row offset, column offset, row slide offset with variation, uniform and directional jitter, uniform and directional scale, Inset with variation, rotate pattern, rotate tile, rotate variation, checkerboard rotate, per tile Value with variation; every randomized value has Set Varying, Variation and Seed. (11 October 2026)\n- Shape: Shape Class (Basic, Marker, Compound), Rectangle with Round Corners, Draw As Filled, Distance, Gradient or Outline, Anti Aliasing and Shape Edge Filter (Houdini 22). (11 October 2026)\n- Pruning and splitting: removal By Tile Order (Default, Reverse, Random, Shift) with Threshold and Negate Selection, every Nth tile, row or column, Checkerboard; Split Tiles with iterations, area threshold, split threshold and orient ratio. (11 October 2026)\n- Grout and bevel: no explicit grout or bevel parameter is documented; the gap comes from Inset, and a bevel comes from the Distance or Gradient draw mode remapped through a profile curve, or from Feather on the tile mask (PROPOSED wiring; whether Distance is expressed in pixels or image units is UNVERIFIED and must be measured once). (11 October 2026)\n\n### 4.4 Measurement capable COPs (11 October 2026)\n\n- Histogram: source and an optional active mask (pixels at or above 0.5); outputs a visualization and a counts layer whose width is the bucket count and whose height is five rows (R, G, B and A counts, then the total processed pixel count); parameters Buckets, Minimum, Maximum, Outside Values Discard or Clamp (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/histogram.html, read). (11 October 2026)\n- Statistics gives average, minimum and maximum of a layer (local list); Statistics by ID writes per island area, minimum and maximum as per pixel Mono layers, has no parameters, and documents no average output (https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/statistic